#: Game/Levels/Specification/L05_StrongEnoughToPinItDown.lean:10
msgid "Here is the sharpest thing you can say about a specification: **it determines the\n"
"implementation.** Not *§0 satisfies it*, but *anything satisfying it is §1*.\n"
"\n"
"That is a much stronger claim, and it is the one that tells you the contract is finished. If\n"
"two different functions could both satisfy it, the contract has not decided something it ought\n"
"to have decided — which is exactly the defect §2 had, and exactly what your\n"
"counterexample in Level 3 exhibited.\n"
"\n"
"So let §3 be *any* function satisfying §4, and prove it agrees with §5\n"
"everywhere.\n"
"\n"
"The proof has the shape you would use on paper. The specification tells you §6 is §7 or\n"
"§8, and that it is at least both. Those three facts, plus knowing which of §9 and §10 is\n"
