msgstr "现在对 §0 与 §1 哪个更大做分情形：§2。"

#. §0: `«{h}» : a ≤ b`
#. §1: `b`
#. §2: `rw [max_eq_right h]`
#. §3: `f «{a}» «{b}» = «{b}»`
#. §4: `«{hcase}»`
#. §5: `«{h1}»`
#. §6: `«{h2}»`
#. §7: `«{h}»`
#. §8: `omega`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L05_StrongEnoughToPinItDown.lean:45
msgid "With §0 the right-hand side is §1, so §2 makes the\n"
"goal §3. Then §4, §5, §6 and §7 together force it, and\n"
"§8 can see that once the disjunction is in the context."
msgstr "有了 §0，右边就是 §1，所以 §2 把目标变成\n"
"§3。接着 §4、§5、§6 和 §7 合起来就逼出了它，而一旦那个析取\n"
"进了上下文，§8 就能看出来。"

#. §0: `rw [max_eq_left h]`
#. §1: `omega`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L05_StrongEnoughToPinItDown.lean:50
msgid "Symmetrically, §0 and then §1."
msgstr "对称地，先 §0 再 §1。"

#. §0: `max`
#. §1: `IsUpperBound`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L05_StrongEnoughToPinItDown.lean:54
msgid "Every implementation of this contract is §0. The specification is tight.\n"
"\n"
"That is the standard you are aiming at, and it is worth saying plainly what it costs. Writing\n"
"a contract that *admits* your implementation is easy and nearly worthless; §1 did\n"
"that. Writing one that *excludes everything else* is the work, and the way to check you have\n"
"done it is to prove uniqueness, or to go hunting for a second implementation and fail.\n"
"\n"
"In practice you often cannot pin a function down completely, and should not want to — a\n"
"specification that permits several correct implementations is what lets an implementation be\n"
"replaced. World 5 is about exactly that freedom. The skill is knowing which parts of behavior\n"
"you meant to fix and which you meant to leave open."
msgstr "这个契约的每个实现都是 §0。规约是紧的。\n"
"\n"
"这就是你要达到的标准，而它的代价值得明说。写一个*容纳*你的实现的契约既容易\n"
"又几乎毫无价值；§1 干的就是这个。写一个*把其他一切都排除在外*的契约才是\n"
"正经活，而检验你是否做到了的办法，是去证明唯一性，或者去找第二个实现却找不到。\n"
"\n"
"实践中你往往钉不死一个函数，也不该想钉死——一个容许好几个正确实现的规约，\n"
"正是实现可以被替换的前提。第五世界讲的就是这份自由。手艺在于知道行为的哪些部分\n"
"你本来要固定，哪些你本来要留白。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:8
msgid "A Specification Nothing Can Satisfy"
msgstr "一个什么也满足不了的规约"

#. §0: `f : List ℕ → ℕ`
#. §1: `f xs < xs.length`
#. §2: `xs`
#. §3: `[]`
#. §4: `f []`
#. §5: `0`
#. §6: `rintro ⟨f, hf⟩`
#. §7: `hf`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:10
msgid "A contract can fail in the other direction too: by demanding more than any program could\n"
"deliver.\n"
"\n"
"Here is one. *Write a function that, given a list of numbers, returns a valid index into it* —\n"
"in other words, a function §0 with §1 for every §2.\n"
"\n"
"It sounds reasonable until you think about the empty list. There are no valid indices into\n"
"§3, so no number §4 can be below §5.\n"
"\n"
"Prove that no such function exists. The statement is a negation, so assume you were handed one\n"
"and derive a contradiction: §6 names the supposed function and its supposed\n"
"property, and then you only have to ask §7 about the empty list."
msgstr "契约也可能朝另一个方向失败：要求的比任何程序能交付的都多。\n"
"\n"
"这里就有一个。*写一个函数，给定一个数的列表，返回一个指向它的合法下标*——\n"
"换句话说，一个函数 §0，对每个 §2 都有 §1。\n"
"\n"
"听起来还算合理，直到你想起空列表。指向 §3 的合法下标一个也没有，\n"
"所以没有任何数 §4 能低于 §5。\n"
"\n"
"证明这样的函数不存在。这个陈述是一个否定，所以假设有人把一个交给了你，\n"
"然后导出矛盾：§6 给那个假想的函数和它假想的性质起名字，\n"
"接着你只需要拿空列表去问 §7。"

#. §0: `no_total_index : ¬∃ f : List ℕ → ℕ, ∀ xs, f xs < xs.length`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:26
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"No total function can return a valid index into every list, because the empty list has none."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"没有全函数能对每个列表都返回一个合法下标，因为空列表一个也没有。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:33
msgid "Show that the contract *returns a valid index into its argument* is unsatisfiable, by\n"
"refuting the existence of any function meeting it."
msgstr "通过否证任何满足它的函数的存在，表明*返回一个指向其参数的合法下标*\n"
"这个契约是不可满足的。"

#. §0: `rintro ⟨f, hf⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:36
msgid "Assume such a function exists and take it apart: §0."
msgstr "假设这样的函数存在，并把它拆开：§0。"

#. §0: `«{hf}»`
#. §1: `have h := hf []`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:38
msgid "§0 is supposed to hold for *every* list. Ask it about the empty one:\n"
"§1."
msgstr "§0 本该对*每个*列表都成立。拿空列表去问它：\n"
"§1。"

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `[].length`
#. §2: `0`
#. §3: `simp at h`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:41
msgid "§0 now says some natural number is smaller than §1, which is §2.\n"
"§3 evaluates the length and finds the contradiction."
msgstr "§0 现在说某个自然数小于 §1，而后者是 §2。\n"
"§3 把长度算出来并找到那个矛盾。"

#. §0: `IsUpperBound`
#. §1: `xs ≠ []`
#. §2: `Option ℕ`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:45
msgid "The contract is not merely hard to meet — it is impossible, and the empty list is the whole\n"
"reason.\n"
"\n"
"Both failures you have now seen come from the same place: the contract and the intention came\n"
"apart at a case nobody pictured. Too weak, and §0 let through a function that\n"
"overshoots. Too strong, and this one lets through nothing at all. Neither mistake is visible\n"
"from reading the proposition; both are visible the moment you ask about the boundary.\n"
"\n"
"The repair here is not to weaken the postcondition but to add a precondition — §1 —\n"
"or to change the return type to §2 so the function can say *no answer*. That second\n"
"option is a real design choice, and World 5 comes back to it."
msgstr "这个契约不只是难以满足——它是不可能满足的，而空列表就是全部原因。\n"
"\n"
"你现在见过的这两种失败都出自同一处：契约与意图在一个谁也没设想过的情形上\n"
"分了家。太弱，于是 §0 放进来一个会超出的函数。太强，于是这一个什么也放不进来。\n"
"两个错误从读命题本身都看不出来；而一旦你去问边界，两个都看得出来。\n"
"\n"
"这里的修补不是削弱后置条件，而是加一个前置条件——§1——\n"
"或者把返回类型改成 §2，好让函数能说*没有答案*。后一个选项是一个真正的\n"
"设计抉择，第五世界会再回到它。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:8
msgid "The Division Contract"
msgstr "除法契约"

#. §0: ```
#. b * q + r = a   and   r < b
#. ```
#. §1: `q = 0, r = 0`
#. §2: `q = 0, r = a`
#. §3: `divmod a b`
#. §4: `(a / b, a % b)`
#. §5: `0 < b`
#. §6: `a % 0 = a`
#. §7: `b = 0`
#. §8: `Nat.div_add_mod a b : b * (a / b) + a % b = a`
#. §9: `Nat.mod_lt a : 0 < b → a % b < b`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:10
msgid "The most famous contract in programming is the one for integer division, and it has two parts\n"
"that only mean something together:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"The first says nothing was lost. The second says the remainder was reduced as far as it goes.\n"
"Drop the first and §1 is fine; drop the second and §2 is fine. Neither\n"
"is division.\n"
"\n"
"§3 returns the pair §4. Prove it satisfies both clauses — under the\n"
"precondition §5, which you should expect by now to be load-bearing. (It is: Lean defines\n"
"§6, so the second clause fails outright at §7.)\n"
"\n"
"Two library facts do the work, and the contract is written in the direction they state it:\n"
"§8 is the first clause and\n"
"§9 is the second."
msgstr "编程里最有名的契约是整数除法的那个，它有两部分，只有合起来才有意义：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"第一条说什么也没丢。第二条说余数已经减到不能再减。去掉第一条，§1 也行；\n"
"去掉第二条，§2 也行。两者都不是除法。\n"
"\n"
"§3 返回序对 §4。证明它满足两条——在前置条件 §5 之下，\n"
"到现在你该料到它是承重的了。（它确实是：Lean 定义 §6，所以第二条在\n"
"§7 时直接不成立。）\n"
"\n"
"两条库里的事实完成这件事，而契约就按它们陈述的方向写：\n"
"§8 是第一条，\n"
"§9 是第二条。"

#. §0: `divmod_correct : 0 < b → b * (divmod a b).1 + (divmod a b).2 = a ∧ (divmod a b).2 < b`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Quotient and remainder satisfy the two-part division contract whenever the divisor is\n"
"positive."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"只要除数为正，商与余数就满足两部分的除法契约。"

#. §0: `divmod`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:40
msgid "Prove that §0 meets the two-part division contract: nothing is lost, and the\n"
"remainder is smaller than the divisor."
msgstr "证明 §0 满足两部分的除法契约：什么也没丢，而且余数小于除数。"

#. §0: `unfold divmod`
#. §1: `a / b`
#. §2: `a % b`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:44
msgid "§0 replaces the pair by its components, so the goal becomes a statement\n"
"about §1 and §2."
msgstr "§0 把序对换成它的两个分量，于是目标变成一个关于 §1 与 §2 的陈述。"

#. §0: `exact ⟨Nat.div_add_mod a b, Nat.mod_lt a h⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:47
msgid "Both halves are now library facts:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "两半现在都是库里的事实：\n"
"§0。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L07_TheDivisionContract.lean:51
msgid "Two obligations, one implementation, and neither obligation would have been enough alone.\n"
"\n"
"That is the pattern you will see again in the capstone. Real contracts are conjunctions,\n"
"because a single property is almost never specific enough to rule out the degenerate\n"
"implementations: returning nothing, returning the input unchanged, returning zero. When you\n"
"write a specification, the useful question is not *is this true of my program* but *what else\n"
"is this true of*."
msgstr "两项义务、一个实现，而两项义务单拿出任何一项都不够。\n"
"\n"
"这正是你在压轴部分会再次见到的模式。真实的契约都是合取，因为单个性质几乎从不\n"
"足够具体到排除那些退化的实现：什么也不返回、原样返回输入、返回零。写规约时，\n"
"有用的问题不是*这对我的程序成立吗*，而是*这还对什么成立*。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:8
msgid "Contracts That Compose"
msgstr "能组合的契约"

#. §0: ```
#. def scaleNonNeg (xs : List Int) : List Int :=
#.   (xs.filter (fun x => 0 ≤ x)).map (fun x => x * 2)
#. ```
#. §1: `filter`
#. §2: `map`
#. §3: `map`
#. §4: `filter`
#. §5: `simp`
#. §6: `map`
#. §7: `filter`
#. §8: `x`
#. §9: `0 ≤ x`
#. §10: `x * 2`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:10
msgid "Programs are built by composing functions, and so are their contracts.\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Two steps: discard the negatives, then double what is left. What can you promise about the\n"
"output? That every element of it is non-negative and even.\n"
"\n"
"Neither half of the program establishes that on its own. §1 contributes the sign;\n"
"§2 contributes the doubling. The proof has to take an arbitrary element of the result,\n"
"trace it back through §3 to the element of the filtered list it came from, and trace that\n"
"back through §4 to learn it was non-negative.\n"
"\n"
"§5 knows how membership in a §6 and a §7 unfolds, so the tracing-back is one\n"
"simp call. What it leaves you is the element §8 it came from, the fact that §9, and the\n"
"knowledge that your element is §10."
msgstr "程序是把函数组合起来搭的，它们的契约也是。\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"两步：丢掉负的，再把剩下的加倍。关于输出你能承诺什么？它的每个元素都非负且是偶数。\n"
"\n"
"程序的哪一半都没法单独确立这一点。§1 贡献了符号；§2 贡献了加倍。\n"
"证明必须取结果中的任意一个元素，经由 §3 回溯到它所来自的、已过滤列表中的那个元素，\n"
"再经由 §4 回溯过去，得知它当初非负。\n"
"\n"
"§5 知道属于 §6 和属于 §7 该如何展开，所以这一路回溯只需一次 simp 调用。\n"
"它留给你的是它所来自的元素 §8、事实 §9，以及你那个元素就是 §10 这件事。"

#. §0: `scaleNonNeg_spec : ∀ y ∈ scaleNonNeg xs, 0 ≤ y ∧ y % 2 = 0`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Every element of the output is non-negative and even."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"输出的每个元素都非负且是偶数。"

#. §0: `scaleNonNeg`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:39
msgid "Prove the contract of §0: every element of its output is non-negative and\n"
"even."
msgstr "证明 §0 的契约：它输出的每个元素都非负且是偶数。"

#. §0: `intro y hy`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:42
msgid "Take an arbitrary element of the output together with the evidence that it is one:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "取输出中的任意一个元素，连同它确实属于输出的证据：§0。"

#. §0: `simp [scaleNonNeg] at hy`
#. §1: `List.map`
#. §2: `List.filter`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:45
msgid "Now unfold what membership in the output means: §0. This\n"
"pushes through both §1 and §2 at once."
msgstr "现在把属于输出意味着什么展开：§0。这一下\n"
"同时穿过 §1 与 §2。"

#. §0: `«{hy}»`
#. §1: `«{y}»`
#. §2: `x * 2`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `x`
#. §5: `obtain ⟨x, hx0, rfl⟩ := hy`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:48
msgid "§0 now says §1 is §2 for some non-negative §3. Name that §4, keep the\n"
"sign fact, and substitute the equation: §5."
msgstr "§0 现在说 §1 对某个非负的 §3 而言就是 §2。给那个 §4 起名字，\n"
"留下符号那条事实，并把等式代入：§5。"

#. §0: `x * 2`
#. §1: `0 ≤ x`
#. §2: `omega`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:51
msgid "Both halves are now arithmetic about §0 given §1, which §2 handles."
msgstr "两半现在都是在 §1 之下关于 §0 的算术，由 §2 处理。"

#. §0: `filter`
#. §1: `map`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L08_ContractsThatCompose.lean:54
msgid "The contract of a composition, assembled from the contracts of its parts.\n"
"\n"
"That is the only way proofs survive contact with real code. Nobody verifies a thousand-line\n"
"function; they verify the twenty functions it calls and compose the results. The composition\n"
"step is where the reasoning happens, and you have just done one: the §0 gave you the\n"
"precondition that the §1's postcondition needed.\n"
"\n"
"World 2 is done. You can write a contract, check it is satisfiable, check it is tight, check\n"
"its assumptions are needed, and assemble it from smaller ones. World 3 is about making the\n"
"proofs themselves reusable."
msgstr "一个复合函数的契约，由它各部分的契约拼装而成。\n"
"\n"
"这是证明在与真实代码接触后得以幸存的唯一方式。没有人去验证一个一千行的函数；\n"
"人们验证它调用的那二十个函数，再把结果组合起来。推理发生在组合这一步上，\n"
"而你刚刚做了一次：§0 给了你 §1 的后置条件所需要的前置条件。\n"
"\n"
"第二世界结束了。你会写契约、会检查它可满足、会检查它紧、会检查它的假设是必要的，\n"
"也会用更小的契约把它拼起来。第三世界讲的是如何让证明本身可以复用。"

#: Game/Levels/Specification.lean:4
msgid "Specify Correct Behavior"
msgstr "规定正确的行为"

#: Game/Levels/Specification.lean:6
msgid "You can now describe what a program does. This world is about saying what it *should* do.\n"
"\n"
"A specification in Lean is an ordinary proposition: a precondition on the input, a\n"
"postcondition relating input to output, and an arrow between them. No separate program logic,\n"
"no Hoare triples — for a pure function the arrow *is* the contract.\n"
"\n"
"The work is rarely in proving a contract. It is in noticing that the contract you wrote is not\n"
"the one you meant. So this world spends its time on the ways a specification goes wrong: too\n"
"weak, and it admits programs you would reject; too strong, and no program can satisfy it; and\n"
"missing an assumption, so that it is simply false.\n"
"\n"
"By the end you will have seen the sharpest standard there is — a contract that pins its\n"
"implementation down completely — and the reason you do not always want it."
msgstr "你现在能描述一个程序做了什么。本世界讲的是说出它*应当*做什么。\n"
"\n"
"Lean 里的规约就是一个普通命题：一个关于输入的前置条件，一个把输入与输出联系起来的\n"
"后置条件，以及它们之间的一个箭头。没有另一套程序逻辑，没有 Hoare 三元组——\n"
"对纯函数而言，那个箭头*就是*契约。\n"
"\n"
"难处很少在于证明一个契约。难处在于察觉你写下的契约并不是你想说的那个。所以本世界\n"
"把时间花在规约会出错的那几种方式上：太弱，它就容纳你会拒绝的程序；太强，就没有程序\n"
"能满足它；还有少了一条假设，于是它干脆就是假的。\n"
"\n"
"到本世界结束时，你会见到最锋利的那个标准——一个把自己的实现完全钉死的契约——\n"
"以及你为什么并不总想要它。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:8
msgid "A Proof That Covers Every List"
msgstr "一个覆盖每个列表的证明"

#. §0: ```
#. def total : List ℕ → ℕ
#.   | [] => 0
#.   | x :: xs => x + total xs
#. ```
#. §1: `++`
#. §2: `total`
#. §3: `[]`
#. §4: `x :: xs`
#. §5: `x`
#. §6: `generalizing`
#. §7: `ys`
#. §8: `ys`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:10
msgid "World 2 proved contracts of functions that look at their input once. This world is about\n"
"functions defined by recursion, and the proofs that follow their shape.\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Here is a fact about it that no finite number of examples establishes: **summing a\n"
"concatenation is the same as summing the pieces and adding.**\n"
"\n"
"The proof is induction on the first list, and it works because §1 recurses the same way\n"
"§2 does. On §3 both sides collapse. On §4 both sides peel off one §5, and what\n"
"is left is the induction hypothesis.\n"
"\n"
"Nothing here needs §6: the statement quantifies over §7, but §8 never changes\n"
"as the recursion proceeds."
msgstr "第二世界证明的是只看输入一次的函数的契约。本世界讲的是由递归定义的函数，\n"
"以及顺着它们的形状走的证明。\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"这是一个关于它的事实，而任何有限多的例子都确立不了它：**把一次拼接求和，\n"
"与把各段分别求和再相加，结果相同。**\n"
"\n"
"证明是对第一个列表做归纳，而它之所以行得通，是因为 §1 递归的方式与 §2 相同。\n"
"在 §3 上两边都塌缩。在 §4 上两边都剥下一个 §5，剩下的就是归纳假设。\n"
"\n"
"这里不需要 §6：陈述对 §7 做了全称量化，但随着递归推进 §8 从不改变。"

#. §0: `total_append : total (xs ++ ys) = total xs + total ys`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The sum of a concatenation is the sum of the parts."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"一次拼接的和，就是各段的和。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:39
msgid "Prove that summing a concatenation gives the same answer as summing each part and\n"
"adding."
msgstr "证明把一次拼接求和，与把每段分别求和再相加，给出相同的答案。"

#. §0: `induction xs with`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:42
msgid "Induct on the first list: §0."
msgstr "对第一个列表做归纳：§0。"

#. §0: `total [] = 0`
#. §1: `simp [total]`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:45
msgid "Appending to the empty list changes nothing, and §0.\n"
"§1 does both."
msgstr "拼到空列表上什么也不改变，而 §0。§1 把两件事一起做了。"

#. §0: `total`
#. §1: `simp [total, ih]`
#. §2: `«{ih}»`
#. §3: `omega`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:49
msgid "Unfold §0 on both sides — §1 also rewrites with the induction\n"
"hypothesis §2 — and then the two sides differ only in how the additions are\n"
"bracketed, which §3 settles."
msgstr "把两边的 §0 都展开——§1 同时还用归纳假设 §2 改写——\n"
"之后两边就只差加法如何加括号了，而 §3 了结它。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L01_InductionOnARecursiveFunction.lean:55
msgid "One theorem, every pair of lists.\n"
"\n"
"Keep an eye on *why* the induction worked: the proof followed the recursion of the function.\n"
"That is the general rule. A function defined by cases on a list is proved correct by induction\n"
"on a list; a function defined by cases on a number, by induction on a number. When a proof by\n"
"induction will not close, the usual reason is that it is inducting on the wrong thing, or\n"
"that the statement is too weak to feed itself — a problem you will meet twice more in this\n"
"world."
msgstr "一个定理，覆盖每一对列表。\n"
"\n"
"留意归纳*为什么*行得通：证明顺着函数的递归走。这是普遍的规律。按列表分情形定义的\n"
"函数，用对列表的归纳来证明正确；按数分情形定义的，就用对数的归纳。当一个归纳证明\n"
"收不了口时，通常的原因是它归纳错了对象，或者陈述太弱以至于喂不饱自己——\n"
"这个问题你在本世界还会再遇到两次。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L02_ALemmaWorthFactoringOut.lean:8
msgid "A Lemma Worth Factoring Out"
msgstr "一条值得提取出来的引理"

#. §0: `total`
#. §1: `reverse`
#. §2: `List.reverse_cons`
