msgstr "反转一个列表不改变它的和。显然，而且不是靠展开什么就能证明的——\n"
"§0 从前端递归，而 §1 把前端挪到后面。\n"
"\n"
"让它行得通的是你刚证过的那个定理。§2 说\n"
"\n"
"§3\n"
"\n"
"于是归纳步骤把目标变成一个关于拼接的陈述，而 §4 正是对付那类陈述的工具。\n"
"\n"
"这是游戏里第一次让先前的结果承重而不只是点缀。它不会是最后一次：本世界余下的部分，\n"
"以及整个第四世界，都是这样搭起来的。"

#. §0: `total_reverse : total xs.reverse = total xs`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L02_ALemmaWorthFactoringOut.lean:29
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Reversing a list leaves its sum unchanged."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"反转一个列表不改变它的和。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L02_ALemmaWorthFactoringOut.lean:36
msgid "Prove that reversing a list does not change its sum, using the concatenation lemma from\n"
"the previous level."
msgstr "用上一关的拼接引理，证明反转一个列表不改变它的和。"

#. §0: `«{xs}»`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L02_ALemmaWorthFactoringOut.lean:39
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L12_ABoundOnTheComparisons.lean:52
msgid "Induct on §0."
msgstr "对 §0 做归纳。"

#. §0: `total []`
#. §1: `rfl`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L02_ALemmaWorthFactoringOut.lean:42
msgid "The reverse of the empty list is itself, so both sides are §0. §1 closes\n"
"it."
msgstr "空列表的反转就是它自己，所以两边都是 §0。§1 关掉它。"

#. §0: `List.reverse_cons`
