#. §0: `List`
#. §1: `LTS`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L08_SortednessSurvivesAnInsertion.lean:83
msgid "The invariant holds: insertion never breaks sortedness.\n"
"\n"
"Compare the shape with the transition-system proofs earlier in this world. There, an invariant\n"
"was a property of states, preserved by each transition. Here it is a property of a data\n"
"structure, preserved by each operation. The second is not a metaphor for the first — it is the\n"
"same idea, and the reason a §0 does not appear as an §1 is only that there is one\n"
"operation and no notion of *the current list* persisting between calls.\n"
"\n"
"In World 4 this lemma becomes one of the two halves of a correctness proof for a real sorting\n"
"algorithm. The other half is the permutation property, and the structure of its proof will\n"
"look familiar."
msgstr "不变式成立：插入从不破坏排好序。\n"
"\n"
"把它的形状和本世界前面那些转移系统的证明比一比。在那里，不变式是状态的性质，\n"
"被每个转移所保持。在这里，它是数据结构的性质，被每个操作所保持。后者不是前者的比喻——\n"
"它就是同一个想法，而一个 §0 之所以没有以 §1 的面目出现，只是因为这里只有一个操作，\n"
"也没有「当前这个列表」在两次调用之间持续存在的概念。\n"
"\n"
"在第四世界，这条引理会成为一个真实排序算法的正确性证明的两半之一。另一半是排列性质，\n"
"而它那个证明的结构你会觉得眼熟。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:8
msgid "An Accumulator Needs Generalizing"
msgstr "累加器需要被推广"

#. §0: `total`
#. §1: `totalTR`
#. §2: ```
#. def totalTR : List ℕ → ℕ → ℕ
#.   | [], acc => acc
#.   | x :: xs, acc => totalTR xs (acc + x)
#. ```
#. §3: `totalTR xs 0 = total xs`
#. §4: `parity_mtr`
#. §5: `totalTR xs (acc + x)`
#. §6: `totalTR xs 0`
#. §7: `0`
#. §8: ```
#. totalTR xs acc = acc + total xs
#. ```
#. §9: `acc = 0`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:10
msgid "Two programs, one answer. §0 recurses and adds on the way back out; §1 carries a\n"
"running accumulator and returns it at the end — which is what a loop compiles to:\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"Prove they agree: §3.\n"
"\n"
"Try it directly and the induction fails, for exactly the reason World 1's §4 failed.\n"
"The recursive call is §5, not §6, so an induction hypothesis\n"
"about the accumulator §7 is useless — you need one about *every* accumulator.\n"
"\n"
"So prove the general statement first:\n"
"\n"
"§8\n"
"\n"
"and read the answer off at §9. This is the same manoeuvre as World 1, in a setting with\n"
"no machine in sight: the accumulator is the state, and a statement about one starting state\n"
"does not induct."
msgstr "两个程序，一个答案。§0 一路递归下去再在回来的路上做加法；§1 带着一个\n"
"运行中的累加器，最后把它返回——这正是循环编译出来的样子：\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"证明它们一致：§3。\n"
"\n"
"直接去试，归纳会失败，原因恰好和第一世界的 §4 失败时一样。\n"
"递归调用是 §5，不是 §6，所以一个关于累加器 §7 的归纳假设毫无用处——\n"
"你需要的是关于*每个*累加器的。\n"
"\n"
"所以先证明一般的陈述：\n"
"\n"
"§8\n"
"\n"
"再在 §9 处把答案读出来。这和第一世界是同一招，只是场景里连机器的影子都没有：\n"
"累加器就是状态，而一个关于单个起始状态的陈述归纳不起来。"

#. §0: `totalTR_eq : totalTR xs 0 = total xs`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:38
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The accumulator version of the sum computes the same answer as the recursive one."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"带累加器的求和版本算出的答案，与递归版本相同。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:45
msgid "Prove that the accumulator version of the sum agrees with the recursive one."
msgstr "证明带累加器的求和版本与递归版本一致。"

#. §0: `have key : ∀ (ys : List ℕ) (acc : ℕ), totalTR ys acc = acc + total ys := by ...`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:47
msgid "State the general version as an auxiliary fact:\n"
"§0"
msgstr "把一般的版本当作辅助事实陈述出来：\n"
"§0"

#. §0: `intro ys`
#. §1: `induction ys with`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:50
msgid "Introduce the list, then induct on it. The accumulator must stay quantified, so do\n"
"not introduce it before the induction: §0, then §1."
msgstr "引入列表，然后对它做归纳。累加器必须保持被量化，所以不要在归纳之前就把它引入：\n"
"先 §0，再 §1。"

#. §0: `intro acc`
#. §1: `simp [totalTR, total]`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:55
msgid "Both sides are the accumulator: §0 and §1."
msgstr "两边都是累加器：§0 与 §1。"

#. §0: `«{ih}»`
#. §1: `acc + x`
#. §2: `intro acc`
#. §3: `simp [totalTR, total, ih]`
#. §4: `omega`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:59
msgid "Now introduce the accumulator for *this* case, unfold one step of each function,\n"
"and rewrite with §0 — which applies at the new accumulator §1, not at the old\n"
"one. §2, then §3, then §4 for the bracketing."
msgstr "现在为*这一种*情形引入累加器，把两个函数各展开一步，\n"
"再用 §0 改写——它适用的是新的累加器 §1，而不是旧的那个。\n"
"先 §2，再 §3，再用 §4 处理括号。"

#. §0: `simpa using key xs 0`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:65
msgid "Read off the case you wanted: §0."
msgstr "把你想要的那个情形读出来：§0。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L09_AnAccumulatorNeedsGeneralizing.lean:68
msgid "The loop and the recursion agree, for every list.\n"
"\n"
"This is **functional equivalence**, and it is the first time in the game two different programs\n"
"have been compared rather than one program compared with a specification. It is the question\n"
"World 5 is entirely about, in settings where the two programs do not even have the same type.\n"
"\n"
"The technique is worth naming, because you have now used it three times: in World 1 for the\n"
"automaton's starting state, in World 1 again for the traffic light, and here for an\n"
"accumulator. Whenever a recursive call changes something the statement mentions, the statement\n"
"must quantify over that thing before the induction, not after."
msgstr "循环与递归一致，对每个列表都如此。\n"
"\n"
"这就是**函数等价**，也是游戏里第一次比较两个不同的程序，而不是拿一个程序去对规约。\n"
"第五世界整个讲的就是这个问题，而且是在两个程序连类型都不相同的场景里。\n"
"\n"
"这个技巧值得点名，因为你现在已经用过三次了：第一世界里为自动机的起始状态，\n"
"第一世界里又为交通灯，以及这里为一个累加器。只要递归调用改变了陈述所提到的某样东西，\n"
"陈述就必须在归纳*之前*对那样东西做量化，而不是之后。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:8
msgid "The Same Argument Without a Machine"
msgstr "同一个论证，只是没有机器"

#. §0: `totalTR xs acc`
#. §1: `acc`
#. §2: `acc ≤ result`
#. §3: `LTS`
#. §4: `mtrInv_of_trInv`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:10
msgid "One last look at the accumulator, because there is an invariant hiding in it.\n"
"\n"
"§0 starts at §1 and never looks back: each recursive call adds something to\n"
"the accumulator, and nothing ever subtracts. So the value it finally returns is at least the\n"
"value it started with.\n"
"\n"
"That is a safety property of a loop — *this variable never decreases* — and the argument is\n"
"the one from the first half of this world. The accumulator is the state. Each recursive call\n"
"is a transition. The property §2 holds trivially when there are no steps left, and\n"
"each step only makes it easier.\n"
"\n"
"What there is **not** is an §3, and so there is no §4 to reach for. You do\n"
"the induction yourself. That is the honest summary of this world: recognise the shape\n"
"everywhere, and reach for the general theorem when the system really is a transition system."
msgstr "再看累加器最后一眼，因为里面藏着一个不变式。\n"
"\n"
"§0 从 §1 开始，并且从不回头：每次递归调用都往累加器上加点什么，\n"
"而从来没有什么被减掉。所以它最终返回的值不小于它出发时的值。\n"
"\n"
"这是一条循环的安全性性质——*这个变量从不下降*——而论证正是本世界前半段的那个。\n"
"累加器是状态。每次递归调用是一个转移。性质 §2 在没有步骤可走时平凡地成立，\n"
"而每一步只会让它更容易成立。\n"
"\n"
"这里**没有**的是一个 §3，所以也没有 §4 可以去拿。归纳得你自己做。\n"
"这就是本世界诚实的总结：到处都认出这个形状，而当系统确实是一个转移系统时，\n"
"就去拿那个一般的定理。"

#. §0: `totalTR_ge_acc : acc ≤ totalTR xs acc`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:28
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The accumulator version of the sum never returns less than it was given."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"带累加器的求和版本，返回的值从不少于它被给定的那个。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:35
msgid "Show that the accumulating sum never returns a value below its starting accumulator."
msgstr "证明带累加器的求和从不返回低于它起始累加器的值。"

#. §0: `induction xs generalizing acc with`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:37
msgid "The accumulator changes as the recursion proceeds, so quantify over it:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "累加器随着递归推进而改变，所以对它做量化：§0。"

#. §0: `simp [totalTR]`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:41
msgid "Nothing left to add; the result is the accumulator itself. §0."
msgstr "没有什么可加的了；结果就是累加器本身。§0。"

#. §0: `«{acc}»`
#. §1: `«{acc}» + «{x}»`
#. §2: `simp only [totalTR]`
#. §3: `exact le_trans (Nat.le_add_right acc x) (ih (acc + x))`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:44
msgid "One step takes the accumulator from §0 to §1, and the induction\n"
"hypothesis bounds the rest from there. §2 exposes the step, and then\n"
"§3 chains the two inequalities."
msgstr "一步把累加器从 §0 带到 §1，而归纳假设从那里起给出其余部分的界。\n"
"§2 把这一步暴露出来，然后 §3 把两个不等式串起来。"

#. §0: `stepL`
#. §1: `total_append`
#. §2: `ins_mem`
#. §3: `mtrInv_of_trInv`
#: Game/Levels/Properties/L10_TheSameArgumentWithoutAMachine.lean:50
msgid "World 3 is done, and it is worth collecting what it was about.\n"
"\n"
"**Induction follows the recursion.** A function defined on lists is proved about by induction\n"
"on lists; an execution built by §0 is proved about by induction on executions.\n"
"\n"
"**Strengthen until it is inductive.** Three times now the statement you wanted was not the\n"
"statement you could prove: the parity automaton's starting state, the two buckets' total, the\n"
"accumulator. Each time the repair was to prove more, not less.\n"
"\n"
"**Factor by shape, not by interest.** §1 and §2 are dull theorems that made\n"
"two interesting ones easy.\n"
"\n"
"**Reuse theorems, not arguments.** §3 did for the room exactly what it did for\n"
"the account, with nothing rewritten. That is what distinguishes a library from a habit.\n"
"\n"
"World 4 puts all four to work on one algorithm."
msgstr "第三世界结束了，值得把它讲的东西收拢一下。\n"
"\n"
"**归纳顺着递归走。**在列表上定义的函数，用对列表的归纳来证明；由 §0 搭起来的执行，\n"
"用对执行的归纳来证明。\n"
"\n"
"**加强到它成为归纳式为止。**到现在已经三次，你想要的陈述不是你能证明的那个：\n"
"奇偶自动机的起始状态、两个桶的总量、累加器。每一次的修补都是多证一点，而不是少证一点。\n"
"\n"
"**按形状提取，不按趣味提取。**§1 和 §2 是两个乏味的定理，却让两个有趣的变得容易。\n"
"\n"
"**复用定理，而不是论证。**§3 为房间做的事，与它为账户做的事一模一样，一个字都没改写。\n"
"这正是库与习惯的区别。\n"
"\n"
"第四世界把这四条一起用在一个算法上。"

#: Game/Levels/Properties.lean:4
msgid "Prove and Reuse Properties"
msgstr "证明并复用性质"

#: Game/Levels/Properties.lean:6
msgid "Worlds 1 and 2 gave you one model and one contract at a time. This world is about proofs that\n"
"do not have to be redone.\n"
"\n"
"The central idea is the **invariant**: a property that holds at the start and survives every\n"
"single step, and therefore holds forever. Stated that way it is a theorem about transition\n"
"systems in general, not about your program — which means somebody can prove it once and\n"
"everybody can use it. CSlib has, and you will prove the same safety property twice, once by\n"
"hand and once by appealing to it, so that the difference is visible rather than asserted.\n"
"\n"
"You will also meet the other kinds of reuse: a helper lemma factored out because the larger\n"
"argument needs it, an invariant of a data structure rather than of a machine, and an\n"
"equivalence between two functions that lets you transport what you know about one onto the\n"
"other.\n"
"\n"
"And you will meet the thing that makes invariant proofs hard — that the property you want is\n"
"usually not the property you can prove, and has to be strengthened first."
msgstr "第一、第二世界每次给你一个模型和一个契约。本世界讲的是不必重做的证明。\n"
"\n"
"核心想法是**不变式**：一个在起点成立、并且挺得过每一步的性质，因而永远成立。\n"
"这样一说，它就是一个关于一般转移系统的定理，而不是关于你的程序的——\n"
"这意味着可以由某个人证明一次，而所有人都能用。CSlib 已经证了，\n"
"而你会把同一条安全性性质证两遍，一遍手工，一遍靠调用它，好让差别是看得见的而不是被断言的。\n"
"\n"
"你还会遇到另外几种复用：因为更大的论证需要而被提取出来的辅助引理；\n"
"属于数据结构而不是属于机器的不变式；以及两个函数之间的等价，\n"
"它让你把关于其中一个所知道的搬运到另一个上。\n"
"\n"
"你还会遇到让不变式证明变难的那件事——你想要的性质通常不是你能证明的那个，\n"
"必须先被加强。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:8
msgid "What Sorted Means"
msgstr "排好序是什么意思"

#. §0: `List.Pairwise r`
#. §1: `r`
#. §2: ```
#. List.Pairwise r []                ↔ True
#. List.Pairwise r (x :: xs)         ↔ (∀ y ∈ xs, r x y) ∧ List.Pairwise r xs
#. ```
#. §3: `List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) xs`
#. §4: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:10
msgid "A capstone needs a subject. This world's is insertion sort, and before proving anything about\n"
"it the contract has to be written down. That turns out to be the part worth slowing over.\n"
"\n"
"*Sorted* in Mathlib v4.35 is not a definition of its own; it is an instance of a more general\n"
"one. §0 says the relation §1 holds between every element and every element\n"
"**after** it:\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"So §3 is exactly *ascending order, duplicates allowed*. Note what it\n"
"does **not** say: nothing about adjacent pairs only, and nothing about which elements are\n"
"present.\n"
"\n"
"Get a feel for it by checking two concrete lists — one that is sorted and one that is not.\n"
"Both sides are decidable, so §4 settles the whole conjunction."
msgstr "压轴需要一个题材。本世界的题材是插入排序，而在证明任何关于它的事情之前，\n"
"契约得先写下来。这件事恰恰值得放慢速度。\n"
"\n"
"Mathlib v4.35 里的*排好序*不是一个独立的定义；它是一个更一般的定义的实例。\n"
"§0 说关系 §1 在每个元素与它**之后**的每个元素之间成立：\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"所以 §3 恰好就是*按升序排好序，允许重复*。注意它**没有**说什么：\n"
"没有说只管相邻的那一对，也没有说哪些元素在场。\n"
"\n"
"检查两个具体的列表来找找感觉——一个排好序，一个没有。两边都是可判定的，\n"
"所以 §4 把整个合取一并了结。"

#. §0: `sorted_examples : List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) [1,2,2,5] ∧ ¬List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) [2,1]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"A worked example and a worked non-example of the sortedness predicate."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"排好序这个谓词的一个正例与一个反例。"

#. §0: `[1,2,2,5]`
#. §1: `[2,1]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:39
msgid "Confirm that §0 satisfies the sortedness predicate and §1 does not."
msgstr "确认 §0 满足排好序这个谓词，而 §1 不满足。"

#. §0: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:42
msgid "Everything here is concrete and decidable. §0."
msgstr "这里的一切都是具体而可判定的。§0。"

#. §0: `[1,2,2,5]`
#. §1: `≤`
#. §2: `[2,1]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L01_WhatSortedMeans.lean:45
msgid "§0 is sorted — equal neighbours are fine, because §1 is reflexive. §2 is not.\n"
"\n"
"That is one half of the contract. The next two levels show that it is only half, by exhibiting\n"
"two programs that each satisfy one half and are plainly not sorting algorithms."
msgstr "§0 是排好序的——相等的相邻元素没问题，因为 §1 是自反的。§2 不是。\n"
"\n"
"这是契约的一半。接下来两关通过举出两个各满足一半、却显然不是排序算法的程序，\n"
"表明它确实只是一半。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:8
msgid "Sorted Is Not Enough"
msgstr "排好序还不够"

#. §0: ```
#. fun xs => []
#. ```
#. §1: `List.Perm`
#. §2: `[]`
#. §3: `[1]`
#. §4: `simp`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:10
msgid "Here is a sorting algorithm that always returns a sorted list:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"It is not a joke so much as a test. If *the output is sorted* were the contract, this would\n"
"satisfy it, and so the contract is too weak — in exactly the sense of World 2, Level 3, and\n"
"you break it the same way: by exhibiting the wrong program.\n"
"\n"
"Produce the function, prove its output is always sorted, and point at an input where the\n"
"output is not a rearrangement of it. §1 is Mathlib's *is a permutation of*; §2 is\n"
"not a permutation of §3, and §4 knows it."
msgstr "这是一个总是返回排好序列表的排序算法：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"与其说它是个笑话，不如说它是个检验。如果契约就是*输出是排好序的*，那它就满足了契约，\n"
"所以这个契约太弱——正是第二世界第三关那个意义上的太弱，而你也用同样的办法把它打破：\n"
"举出那个错的程序。\n"
"\n"
"把这个函数造出来，证明它的输出总是排好序的，再指出一个输入，使得输出并不是它的重排。\n"
"§1 是 Mathlib 的*是……的一个排列*；§2 不是 §3 的排列，而 §4 知道这一点。"

#. §0: `sorted_not_enough : ∃ f, (∀ xs, List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) (f xs)) ∧ ∃ xs, ¬(f xs).Perm xs`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:27
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Sortedness alone does not specify sorting: a function returning the empty list satisfies it."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"单有排好序并不能刻画排序：一个返回空列表的函数就满足它。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:34
msgid "Show that sortedness alone is too weak a contract for a sorting function, by exhibiting\n"
"a function that satisfies it and is not a sorting function."
msgstr "通过举出一个满足它却不是排序函数的函数，表明单有排好序对排序函数而言是太弱的契约。"

#. §0: `refine ⟨fun _ => [], fun xs => by simp, [1], ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:38
msgid "Supply the function, its sortedness proof, and the offending input in one go:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "一口气把函数、它的排好序证明，以及那个出问题的输入都给出来：§0。"

#. §0: `[]`
#. §1: `[1]`
#. §2: `simp`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:41
msgid "What remains is that §0 is not a permutation of §1, which §2 decides."
msgstr "剩下的是 §0 不是 §1 的排列，这由 §2 判定。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L02_SortedIsNotEnough.lean:44
msgid "Half a contract admits a program that throws its input away.\n"
"\n"
"The lesson is the one from World 2 restated on a bigger example: ask of every specification\n"
"what else satisfies it. And the degenerate programs are always the same few — return nothing,\n"
"return the input, return a constant — so they are cheap to check against."
msgstr "半个契约容纳了一个把自己输入丢掉的程序。\n"
"\n"
"这条教训就是第二世界那条，只是换到了更大的例子上：对每个规约都问一句还有什么满足它。\n"
"而那些退化的程序来来去去总是那几个——什么也不返回、原样返回输入、返回一个常数——\n"
"所以拿它们来对照的代价很低。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:8
msgid "A Permutation Is Not Enough"
msgstr "是个排列也还不够"

#. §0: ```
#. fun xs => xs
#. ```
#. §1: `id`
#. §2: `fun _ => []`
#. §3: `List.Perm.refl`
#. §4: `[2,1]`
#. §5: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:10
msgid "Now the other half, and the other degenerate program:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Its output is always a permutation of its input — the identity permutation. So *the output is\n"
"a rearrangement of the input* is too weak as well.\n"
"\n"
"Neither clause is redundant and neither is sufficient. **Sorted** rules out §1; **permutation**\n"
"rules out §2. Only the conjunction says sorting, and that is why the capstone of\n"
"this world proves two things rather than one.\n"
"\n"
"§3 gives the permutation half. For the counterexample, §4 is unsorted, and\n"
"§5 can see that."
msgstr "现在轮到另一半，以及另一个退化的程序：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"它的输出总是输入的一个排列——恒等排列。所以*输出是输入的一个重排*同样太弱。\n"
"\n"
"两条都不冗余，两条也都不充分。**排好序**排除掉 §1；**排列**排除掉 §2。\n"
"只有合取才说出了排序，而这正是本世界的压轴要证两件事而不是一件事的原因。\n"
"\n"
"§3 给出排列那一半。至于反例，§4 没有排好序，而 §5 看得出来。"

#. §0: `perm_not_enough : ∃ f, (∀ xs, (f xs).Perm xs) ∧ ∃ xs, ¬List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) (f xs)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:29
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Being a permutation alone does not specify sorting: the identity function satisfies it."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"单是一个排列并不能刻画排序：恒等函数就满足它。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:36
msgid "Show that the permutation clause alone is too weak, by exhibiting a function that\n"
"satisfies it and is not a sorting function."
msgstr "通过举出一个满足它却不是排序函数的函数，表明单有排列这一条太弱。"

#. §0: `refine ⟨id, fun xs => List.Perm.refl _, [2,1], ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:40
msgid "The identity function, its permutation proof, and an unsorted input:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "恒等函数、它的排列证明，以及一个没有排好序的输入：§0。"

#. §0: `[2,1]`
#. §1: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:43
msgid "§0 is concretely unsorted, so §1."
msgstr "§0 具体地没有排好序，所以 §1。"

#. §0: ```
#. List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) (sort xs)  ∧  (sort xs).Perm xs
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L03_APermutationIsNotEnough.lean:46
msgid "The contract is settled:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Two obligations, each ruling out a program the other admits. Everything else in this world is\n"
"the work of discharging them for a real algorithm — first one you can see all of, then CSlib's\n"
"cost-annotated one."
msgstr "契约定下来了：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"两项义务，各自排除掉对方所容纳的一个程序。本世界其余的一切，都是为一个真实的算法把它们\n"
"了结的工作——先是一个你能从头看到尾的，然后是 CSlib 那个带开销标注的。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:8
msgid "Insertion Is a Permutation"
msgstr "插入是一个排列"

#. §0: `ins`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `xs`
#. §3: `a :: xs`
#. §4: `ins_mem`
#. §5: `List.Perm`
#. §6: `a ≤ x`
#. §7: `a :: x :: xs`
#. §8: `a > x`
#. §9: `x :: ins a xs`
#. §10: `ins a xs`
#. §11: `a :: xs`
#. §12: `x :: ins a xs`
#. §13: `x :: a :: xs`
#. §14: `a :: x :: xs`
#. §15: `List.Perm.cons`
#. §16: `List.Perm.swap`
#. §17: `List.Perm.trans`
#. §18: `h.trans`
#. §19: `trans`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:10
msgid "World 3 proved that §0 preserves sortedness. That is the first obligation. Here is the\n"
"second, for the same operation: **inserting §1 into §2 produces a rearrangement of\n"
"§3.**\n"
"\n"
"§4 was close but not enough. It says which elements are present; a permutation also has\n"
"to account for how many times each occurs. §5 tracks that.\n"
"\n"
"The induction has the same two branches as before. When §6 the result is literally\n"
"§7, so there is nothing to rearrange. When §8 the result is §9,\n"
"and the induction hypothesis says §10 is a rearrangement of §11 — so\n"
"§12 rearranges to §13, which is §14 with the first two\n"
"elements swapped.\n"
"\n"
"Three lemmas do it: §15 puts the same element on the front of both sides,\n"
"§16 exchanges the first two, and §17 chains them. Write them out by\n"
"name rather than with dot notation — §18 is shorter, but the game resolves the field of a\n"
"projection as a name in its own right, and §19 on its own is a different theorem."
msgstr "第三世界证明了 §0 保持排好序。那是第一项义务。这里是同一个操作的第二项：\n"
"**把 §1 插进 §2 得到的是 §3 的一个重排。**\n"
"\n"
"§4 很接近，但还不够。它说的是哪些元素在场；而一个排列还得交代每个元素出现几次。\n"
"§5 记录这件事。\n"
"\n"
"归纳和之前一样有那两个分支。当 §6 时结果字面上就是 §7，所以没有什么要重排的。\n"
"当 §8 时结果是 §9，而归纳假设说 §10 是 §11 的一个重排——于是\n"
"§12 重排成 §13，也就是把 §14 的前两个元素对调。\n"
"\n"
"三条引理完成这件事：§15 在两边前面放上同一个元素，§16 对调前两个，\n"
"而 §17 把它们串起来。把它们按名字写出来，不要用点记号——§18 更短，\n"
"但游戏会把投影的字段当作一个独立的名字去解析，而单独的 §19 是另一个定理。"

#. §0: `ins_perm : (ins a xs).Perm (a :: xs)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:31
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Insertion rearranges rather than changes: the result is a permutation of the input with the\n"
"new element added."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"插入是重排而不是改动：结果是输入添上新元素后的一个排列。"

#. §0: `a`
#. §1: `xs`
#. §2: `a :: xs`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:39
msgid "Prove that inserting §0 into §1 yields a permutation of §2."
msgstr "证明把 §0 插进 §1 得到的是 §2 的一个排列。"

#. §0: `[a]`
#. §1: `a :: []`
#. §2: `simp [ins]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:44
msgid "Inserting into the empty list gives §0, which is §1. §2."
msgstr "插进空列表得到 §0，也就是 §1。§2。"

#. §0: `by_cases hax : a ≤ x`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:47
msgid "Split on the comparison: §0."
msgstr "对那个比较做分情形：§0。"

#. §0: `a`
#. §1: `simp only [ins, hax]`
#. §2: `exact List.Perm.refl _`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:49
msgid "§0 goes straight to the front, so the two lists are equal and nothing needs\n"
"rearranging. §1, then §2."
msgstr "§0 直接排到最前面，所以两个列表相等，没有什么要重排的。先 §1，再 §2。"

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `simp only [ins, hax]`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `exact List.Perm.trans (List.Perm.cons x ih) (List.Perm.swap a x xs)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:53
msgid "§0 stays in front and §1 is inserted into the tail. §2,\n"
"then put §3 on the front of the induction hypothesis and swap the first two elements:\n"
"§4."
msgstr "§0 留在前面，而 §1 被插进尾部。先 §2，然后在归纳假设前面放上 §3，\n"
"再把前两个元素对调：§4。"

#. §0: `ins_mem`
#. §1: `≤`
#. §2: `ins`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L04_InsertionIsAPermutation.lean:59
msgid "Insertion satisfies both obligations now: it keeps the list sorted, and it loses nothing.\n"
"\n"
"The two proofs looked quite different — the sortedness one needed §0 and transitivity\n"
"of §1, this one needed the permutation algebra — but they share a structure, because both\n"
"follow the recursion of §2. That is the reward for defining the operation cleanly: every\n"
"property of it is proved by the same case split.\n"
"\n"
"Two more levels lift these from the single insertion to the whole sort."
msgstr "插入现在满足两项义务了：它保持列表排好序，而且什么也没丢。\n"
"\n"
"这两个证明看起来相当不同——排好序那个需要 §0 以及 §1 的传递性，这一个需要排列代数——\n"
"但它们共享一个结构，因为两者都顺着 §2 的递归走。这是把操作定义干净的回报：\n"
"关于它的每条性质都用同一次分情形来证明。\n"
"\n"
"再有两关，就把这些从单次插入提升到整个排序。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:8
msgid "The Whole Sort Is Sorted"
msgstr "整个排序是排好序的"

#. §0: ```
#. def isort : List ℕ → List ℕ
#.   | [] => []
#.   | x :: xs => ins x (isort xs)
#. ```
#. §1: `ins_sorted`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:10
msgid "Insertion sort is insertion, repeated:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Sort the tail, then insert the head into the result. Prove the whole thing returns a sorted\n"
"list.\n"
"\n"
"This is where the preparation pays. The induction hypothesis says the sorted tail is sorted;\n"
"§1 says inserting into a sorted list keeps it sorted; and that is the entire\n"
"argument. There is no new reasoning about order anywhere in this level — it was all done once,\n"
"for one insertion, in World 3.\n"
"\n"
"That is what *compositional* means, and it is the only reason verifying real programs is\n"
"possible at all."
msgstr "插入排序就是反复插入：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"先排好尾部，再把表头插进结果里。证明整个东西返回一个排好序的列表。\n"
"\n"
"准备工作在这里得到回报。归纳假设说排好序的尾部是排好序的；§1 说插进一个排好序的列表\n"
"会让它仍然排好序；而这就是全部的论证。本关里任何地方都没有关于顺序的新推理——\n"
"那些在第三世界已经为单次插入一次做完了。\n"
"\n"
"这就是*可组合*的意思，也是验证真实程序根本得以可能的唯一原因。"

#. §0: `isort_sorted : (isort xs).Pairwise (· ≤ ·)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Insertion sort returns a sorted list."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"插入排序返回一个排好序的列表。"

#. §0: `isort`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:39
msgid "Prove that §0 always returns a sorted list."
msgstr "证明 §0 总是返回一个排好序的列表。"

#. §0: `simp [isort]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:44
msgid "Sorting nothing gives nothing, and the empty list is sorted. §0."
msgstr "什么也不排就什么也得不到，而空列表是排好序的。§0。"

#. §0: `ins x (isort xs)`
#. §1: `«{ih}»`
#. §2: `ins_sorted`
#. §3: `exact ins_sorted x (isort xs) ih`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:47
msgid "The result is §0. The tail is sorted by §1, and §2\n"
"says inserting into a sorted list leaves it sorted:\n"
"§3."
msgstr "结果是 §0。尾部由 §1 排好序，而 §2 说插进一个排好序的列表会让它仍然排好序：\n"
"§3。"

#. §0: `ins_sorted`
#. §1: `ins_mem`
#. §2: `List.pairwise_cons`
#. §3: `isort`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L05_TheWholeSortIsSorted.lean:52
msgid "The first of the two obligations, for the whole algorithm, in three lines.\n"
"\n"
"Count what those three lines rest on: an induction here, §0 from World 3, §1\n"
"underneath that, and §2 from the library. Four small results, each proved\n"
"where it was easiest, composing into a statement about an algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"Had you tried to prove this directly about §3, you would have had to do all of it at\n"
"once, inside a single induction, with the comparison case split nested inside the list case\n"
"split. That proof exists and people write it. It is about four times as long and nobody can\n"
"read it."
msgstr "两项义务中的第一项，对整个算法而言，三行搞定。\n"
"\n"
"数一数那三行靠的是什么：这里的一次归纳、第三世界的 §0、它下面的 §1，\n"
"以及库里的 §2。四个小结果，各自在最容易证的地方证出来，组合成一个关于算法的陈述。\n"
"\n"
"假如你当初试着直接对 §3 证明这件事，你就得一次把这一切都做完，塞在同一次归纳里面，\n"
"而且比较的分情形还嵌套在列表的分情形里面。那个证明是存在的，也有人写。\n"
"它大约长四倍，而且没人读得下去。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:8
msgid "The Whole Sort Is a Permutation"
msgstr "整个排序是一个排列"

#. §0: `isort (x :: xs)`
#. §1: `ins x (isort xs)`
#. §2: `ins_perm`
#. §3: `x :: isort xs`
#. §4: `isort xs`
#. §5: `xs`
#. §6: `x :: isort xs`
#. §7: `x :: xs`
#. §8: `List.Perm.cons`
#. §9: `::`
#. §10: `List.Perm.trans`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:10
msgid "The same lift, for the other obligation.\n"
"\n"
"§0 is §1. By §2 that is a permutation of\n"
"§3, and by the induction hypothesis §4 is a permutation of §5, so\n"
"§6 is a permutation of §7. Chain the two and you are done.\n"
"\n"
"§8 lifts a permutation under a §9, and §10 chains. Both appeared\n"
"in Level 4; this level is about putting them together in the other order."
msgstr "另一项义务的同样一次提升。\n"
"\n"
"§0 就是 §1。由 §2，它是 §3 的一个排列；而由归纳假设，§4 是 §5 的一个排列，\n"
"所以 §6 是 §7 的一个排列。把两者串起来就完事了。\n"
"\n"
"§8 把一个排列在 §9 之下提升，而 §10 做串接。两者都在第四关出现过；\n"
"本关讲的是把它们按另一个顺序拼起来。"

#. §0: `isort_perm : (isort xs).Perm xs`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:22
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Insertion sort returns a permutation of its input."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"插入排序返回其输入的一个排列。"

#. §0: `isort`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:29
msgid "Prove that §0 always returns a permutation of its input."
msgstr "证明 §0 总是返回其输入的一个排列。"

#. §0: `simp [isort]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:34
msgid "Sorting nothing gives nothing. §0."
msgstr "什么也不排就什么也得不到。§0。"

#. §0: `ins_perm x (isort xs)`
#. §1: `ins x (isort xs)`
#. §2: `x :: isort xs`
#. §3: `List.Perm.cons x «{ih}»`
#. §4: `x :: xs`
#. §5: `exact List.Perm.trans (ins_perm x (isort xs)) (List.Perm.cons x ih)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:37
msgid "Two steps, chained. §0 moves from §1 to\n"
"§2, and §3 moves from there to §4:\n"
"§5."
msgstr "两步，串起来。§0 把你从 §1 带到 §2，而 §3 从那里带到 §4：§5。"

#. §0: `isort`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L06_TheWholeSortIsAPermutation.lean:42
msgid "Both obligations are now proved for §0, separately.\n"
"\n"
"Separately is how they should be proved — they are about different things, and mixing them\n"
"would make both arguments worse. But separately is not how they should be *stated*: a caller\n"
"wants one theorem it can rely on. That is the next level, and it is shorter than this one."
msgstr "两项义务现在都为 §0 证明了，各自分开地。\n"
"\n"
"分开正是它们该被证明的方式——它们讲的是不同的事情，混在一起会让两个论证都变糟。\n"
"但分开不是它们该被*陈述*的方式：调用方想要一个可以依赖的定理。那就是下一关，\n"
"而且它比这一关更短。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:8
msgid "Both Obligations at Once"
msgstr "一次把两项义务都办了"

#. §0: ```
#. List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) (isort xs)  ∧  (isort xs).Perm xs
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:10
msgid "You have the two halves. State the contract from Level 3 and discharge it.\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"The proof is the pair of theorems you already have. That is deliberate: a correctness theorem\n"
"should be a thin statement over results proved elsewhere, because it is the statement users\n"
"read and the statement that must not drift. If this level were hard, the decomposition would\n"
"be wrong."
msgstr "两半你都有了。把第三关的契约陈述出来并了结它。\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"证明就是你已经有的那一对定理。这是有意的：一个正确性定理应当是架在别处证出的结果之上的\n"
"一层薄薄的陈述，因为它是用户会读的那个陈述，也是不能走样的那个陈述。\n"
"如果这一关很难，那说明分解做错了。"

#. §0: `isort_correct : List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·) (isort xs) ∧ (isort xs).Perm xs`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:24
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Insertion sort is correct: its output is sorted and is a permutation of its input."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"插入排序是正确的：它的输出排好序，并且是其输入的一个排列。"

#. §0: `isort`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:31
msgid "Prove §0 correct against the full two-part contract."
msgstr "对照完整的两部分契约，证明 §0 正确。"

#. §0: `exact ⟨isort_sorted xs, isort_perm xs⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:34
msgid "Both halves are already theorems. §0."
msgstr "两半都已经是定理了。§0。"

#. §0: `ins`
#. §1: `isort`
#. §2: `List.insertionSortM`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L07_BothObligationsAtOnce.lean:37
msgid "A verified sorting algorithm, from scratch, in four levels and a lemma borrowed from World 3.\n"
"\n"
"Now the question this world exists to ask. You wrote §0 and §1 yourself, and the proofs\n"
"followed their structure. What happens when the algorithm is not yours — when it comes from a\n"
"library, is written over an arbitrary monad so that it can be instrumented, and does not look\n"
"like anything you can induct on directly?\n"
"\n"
"That is CSlib's §2, and the rest of this world is about it."
msgstr "一个从零写起的、被验证过的排序算法，用了四关，外加一条从第三世界借来的引理。\n"
"\n"
"现在轮到本世界存在的理由那个问题了。§0 和 §1 是你自己写的，证明也顺着它们的结构走。\n"
"那么当算法不是你写的时候会怎样——当它来自一个库，为了能被插桩而写在任意 monad 之上，\n"
"而且看起来根本不像你能直接对之归纳的任何东西？\n"
"\n"
"那就是 CSlib 的 §2，而本世界余下的部分讲的就是它。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:9
msgid "The Same Algorithm, over a Monad"
msgstr "同一个算法，写在 monad 之上"

#. §0: ```
#. def List.insertionSortM (r : α → α → m Bool) : List α → m (List α)
#.   | [] => pure []
#.   | b :: l => do List.orderedInsertM r b (← List.insertionSortM r l)
#. ```
#. §1: `r`
#. §2: `m`
#. §3: `Id`
#. §4: `Cslib.Algorithms.Lean.TimeM ℕ`
#. §5: ```
#. def cmpCost (a b : ℕ) : TimeM ℕ Bool := do
#.   TimeM.tick 1
#.   return (decide (a ≤ b))
#. 
#. def timedSort (xs : List ℕ) : TimeM ℕ (List ℕ) := List.insertionSortM cmpCost xs
#. ```
#. §6: `(timedSort xs).ret`
#. §7: `(timedSort xs).time`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:11
msgid "CSlib's insertion sort is written once, over an arbitrary monad:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"The comparison §1 is a monadic operation, so *what a comparison costs* is a parameter.\n"
"Instantiate §2 at §3 and you get an ordinary sort. Instantiate it at\n"
"§4 — a pair of a result and an accumulated cost — and every\n"
"comparison is charged:\n"
"\n"
"§5\n"
"\n"
"§6 is the sorted list and §7 is the number of comparisons\n"
"it performed.\n"
"\n"
"Be clear about what that number is. It is **not** a measurement. It is the value of an\n"
"annotation in a declared cost model — *a comparison costs 1, everything else is free* — which\n"
"you chose and which the library takes on trust. The theorem you prove about it is a theorem\n"
"about the model.\n"
"\n"
"Start by running it."
msgstr "CSlib 的插入排序只写了一次，写在任意 monad 之上：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"比较 §1 是一个 monad 运算，所以*一次比较要花多少*是一个参数。\n"
"把 §2 实例化到 §3 就得到一个普通的排序。把它实例化到 §4——\n"
"一个由结果和累计开销构成的序对——每次比较就都被计费：\n"
"\n"
"§5\n"
"\n"
"§6 是排好序的列表，而 §7 是它所做的比较次数。\n"
"\n"
"要把那个数字是什么说清楚。它**不是**测量值。它是你所声明的开销模型里一个标注的取值——\n"
"*一次比较花 1，别的都免费*——这个模型是你选的，而库对它照单全收。\n"
"你关于它证明的定理，是关于这个模型的定理。\n"
"\n"
"先让它跑起来。"

#. §0: `timedSort_run : (timedSort [3,1,2]).ret = [1,2,3]`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:45
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The cost-annotated sort computes what a sort should compute."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"带开销标注的排序算出了一个排序该算出的东西。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:52
msgid "Run the cost-annotated sort on a concrete list and confirm the result."
msgstr "在一个具体的列表上运行带开销标注的排序，并确认结果。"

#. §0: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:54
msgid "Concrete input, concrete output, so this is a computation: §0."
msgstr "具体的输入、具体的输出，所以这是一次计算：§0。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L08_TheSameAlgorithmOverAMonad.lean:57
msgid "It sorts. On one input.\n"
"\n"
"You are back where World 1 started, and for the same reason: the first thing to establish about\n"
"an unfamiliar definition is what it does, and the cheapest way to find out is to run it. The\n"
"difference is that you now know exactly how far that gets you.\n"
"\n"
"The next level runs it twice, and the two answers differ in a way worth noticing."
msgstr "它确实排序。在一个输入上。\n"
"\n"
"你回到了第一世界的起点，而且是出于同样的理由：关于一个陌生定义，首先要弄清的是它做什么，\n"
"而最省事的办法是让它跑一下。不同的是，你现在清楚地知道这能带你走多远。\n"
"\n"
"下一关让它跑两次，而那两个答案的差别值得注意。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:9
msgid "Best Case and Worst Case"
msgstr "最好情形与最坏情形"

#. §0: `.ret`
#. §1: `.time`
#. §2: `n`
#. §3: `n - 1`
#. §4: `O(·)`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:11
msgid "§0 is what the algorithm computes. §1 is what it cost.\n"
"\n"
"Insertion sort's cost depends on the input, not only its size. On an already-sorted list every\n"
"insertion stops at the first comparison, so sorting §2 elements costs §3. On a\n"
"reverse-sorted list every insertion walks the whole prefix, so the cost grows quadratically.\n"
"\n"
"Both lists below have four elements. Show that the second costs strictly more than the first.\n"
"\n"
"This is the observation that makes a cost model worth having: it distinguishes inputs that an\n"
"§4 statement about the worst case does not."
msgstr "§0 是算法算出的东西。§1 是它花掉的东西。\n"
"\n"
"插入排序的开销取决于输入，而不只取决于输入的大小。在一个已排好序的列表上，每次插入都在\n"
"第一次比较时就停下，所以排 §2 个元素花 §3。在一个逆序的列表上，每次插入都要走完整个前缀，\n"
"于是开销按平方增长。\n"
"\n"
"下面两个列表都有四个元素。表明第二个严格地花得更多。\n"
"\n"
"正是这个观察让一个开销模型值得拥有：它区分开那些关于最坏情形的 §4 陈述所区分不开的输入。"

#. §0: `timedSort_cost_differs : (timedSort [1,2,3,4]).time < (timedSort [4,3,2,1]).time`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:25
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Insertion sort's comparison count depends on the input, not only on its length."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"插入排序的比较次数取决于输入，而不只取决于它的长度。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:32
msgid "Show that the cost-annotated sort charges strictly more for a reverse-sorted list than\n"
"for an already-sorted list of the same length."
msgstr "表明对同样长度的列表，带开销标注的排序对逆序的那个收费严格多于对已排好序的那个。"

#. §0: `decide`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:36
msgid "Both costs are concrete numbers, so this is a computation: §0."
msgstr "两个开销都是具体的数，所以这是一次计算：§0。"

#. §0: `.ret`
#. §1: `.time`
#: Game/Levels/Verification/L09_BestCaseAndWorstCase.lean:39
msgid "Three comparisons against six.\n"
"\n"
"Keep the two fields apart in your head, because they behave very differently under the\n"
"reasoning that follows. §0 is the answer, and the answer does not depend on the\n"
"instrumentation — which is exactly what the next level turns into a theorem. §1 is the\n"
"instrumentation, and nothing about the plain algorithm can tell you anything about it.\n"
"\n"
"That asymmetry is the shape of the rest of this world: one obligation that transfers for free,\n"
"and one that has to be proved where it lives."
msgstr "三次比较对六次。\n"
"\n"
"把这两个字段在脑子里分开，因为在接下来的推理下它们的表现非常不同。§0 是答案，\n"
"而答案不依赖于插桩——这恰恰就是下一关要变成定理的东西。§1 是插桩，\n"
"而关于那个朴素算法的任何事情都没法告诉你关于它的任何事情。\n"
"\n"
"这份不对称就是本世界余下部分的形状：一项义务白白转移过来，另一项必须在它所在的地方证明。"

#: Game/Levels/Verification/L10_DiscardingTheCost.lean:9
msgid "Discarding the Cost"
msgstr "把开销丢掉"

#. §0: `timedSort`
#. §1: `List.insertionSortM`
#. §2: `TimeM ℕ`
#. §3: `List.insertionSort`
#. §4: `pure`
#. §5: `>>=`
#. §6: `do`
#. §7: ```
#. TimeM.isMonadHom_pure_ret
#.   : IsMonadHom (TimeM T) Id (fun x => pure x.ret)
#. 
#. IsMonadHom.map_listInsertionSortM
#.   : f (List.insertionSortM r xs) = List.insertionSortM (fun x y => f (r x y)) xs
#. ```
#. §8: `pure`
#. §9: `decide (x ≤ y) = true`
#. §10: `(· ≤ ·)`
