"附带事实。别的一切——一次插入是线性的、一次 bind 的开销相加、递归把它们累积起来——\n"
"都是你自己确立的，用的恰好是第一到第三世界的技术：顺着递归走、加强到假设可用为止、\n"
"在需要它的那次归纳之前把配料提取出来。\n"
"\n"
"关于你所证明的东西，最后两点提醒。这个界是平方的，而插入排序在最坏情形下确实是平方的，\n"
"但 §0 并不紧——真正的最坏情形是 §1，而证明*那个*是另一次不同且更难的归纳。\n"
"还有，被数出来的是你所声明的模型里的比较次数，不是机器上的时间。§2 自己的文档对此说得很直白：\n"
"那些标注是被信任的，不是被验证的。开销模型和任何别的规约一样是一个规约，\n"
"也和任何别的规约一样，可能对它本来要描述的东西说错话。\n"
"\n"
"这就是核心路线。第五世界是可选的，它问一个这里从未触及的问题：一个实现何时可以替换另一个？"

#: Game/Levels/Verification.lean:4
msgid "Verify a Complete Implementation"
msgstr "验证一个完整的实现"

#. §0: `List.insertionSortM`
#: Game/Levels/Verification.lean:6
msgid "Everything so far has been one technique at a time. This world puts them together on one\n"
"algorithm, and follows it all the way through.\n"
"\n"
"It starts with the contract, because that is where verification starts: what does *sorted*\n"
"mean, and why is it not enough on its own? Two degenerate programs will show you that it takes\n"
"two obligations to say *sorting*.\n"
"\n"
"Then insertion sort, twice. First a version you write and prove yourself, so that every step\n"
"of the argument is visible. Then CSlib's §0, which is written over a monad\n"
"so that the same code can run plainly or with its comparisons counted — and which you will\n"
"relate to Mathlib's ordinary sort by a general theorem about monad homomorphisms, getting both\n"
"correctness obligations for almost nothing.\n"
"\n"
"The world ends where that shortcut runs out. Cost is exactly the information the shortcut\n"
"discards, so a bound on the number of comparisons has to be proved from first principles, in\n"
"the cost monad, by an induction of your own. Cost here is something you *model* and prove\n"
"about, never something measured."
msgstr "到目前为止每次都只有一种技术。本世界把它们合到一个算法上，并一路跟到底。\n"
"\n"
"它从契约开始，因为验证就是从那里开始的：*排好序*是什么意思，它单独为什么不够？\n"
"两个退化的程序会让你看到，说出*排序*需要两项义务。\n"
"\n"
"然后是插入排序，两遍。先是一个你自己写、自己证的版本，好让论证的每一步都看得见。\n"
"然后是 CSlib 的 §0，它写在 monad 之上，使得同一段代码既能朴素地跑，也能带着比较计数跑——\n"
"而你会用一条关于 monad 同态的一般定理把它与 Mathlib 普通的排序联系起来，\n"
"几乎不费力地拿到两项正确性义务。\n"
"\n"
"本世界结束在那条捷径用尽的地方。开销恰恰是那条捷径所丢弃的信息，所以一个关于比较次数的界\n"
"必须从第一性原理出发，在开销 monad 里，用你自己的一次归纳证出来。这里的开销是你*建模*\n"
"并证明的东西，绝不是被测量出来的东西。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:8
msgid "The Same Answer, Where It Matters"
msgstr "在要紧的地方给出同样的答案"

#. §0: ```
#. def lookupRaw     (xs : List ℕ) (i : ℕ) : ℕ        := xs.getD i 0
#. def lookupChecked (xs : List ℕ) (i : ℕ) : Option ℕ := xs[i]?
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:10
msgid "*Optional branch.* Nothing in the core path depends on this world, and you can come back to it\n"
"whenever you like.\n"
"\n"
"The question it asks is the one that comes up every time a component is rewritten: **may I\n"
"replace this with that?** The answer is almost never a plain yes, and the interesting part is\n"
"what qualifies it.\n"
"\n"
"Start with the smallest version. Two ways to read an element out of a list:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"The first is what a language without bounds checks gives you: out of range it quietly hands\n"
"back a default. The second reports the failure instead.\n"
"\n"
"They do not even have the same return type, so *equal* is not available. What is available is\n"
"a claim about the inputs where both behave: **when the index is in range, the checked version\n"
"returns exactly what the raw version returns.** That is **conditional functional equivalence**,\n"
"and the condition is the whole content of it."
msgstr "*可选分支。*核心路线没有任何部分依赖本世界，你可以随时再回来。\n"
"\n"
"它问的问题，是每次有组件被重写时都会冒出来的那个：**我可以拿这个替换那个吗？**\n"
"答案几乎从来不是一句干脆的「可以」，而有意思的部分正是那些限定条件。\n"
"\n"
"从最小的版本开始。从列表里读出一个元素的两种办法：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"第一种是不做边界检查的语言给你的：越界时它悄悄递回一个默认值。第二种则报告这次失败。\n"
"\n"
"它们连返回类型都不相同，所以*相等*这个说法用不上。用得上的是一个关于两者都正常工作的\n"
"那些输入的论断：**当下标在范围内时，带检查的版本返回的恰好就是不带检查的版本所返回的。**\n"
"这就是**条件函数等价**，而那个条件就是它的全部内容。"

#. §0: `lookupChecked_agrees : i < xs.length → lookupChecked xs i = some (lookupRaw xs i)`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:35
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"On indices that are in range, the checked lookup returns exactly the unchecked one's answer."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"在范围内的下标上，带检查的读取返回的恰好是不带检查那个的答案。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:42
msgid "Show that on in-range indices the checked lookup agrees with the unchecked one."
msgstr "证明在范围内的下标上，带检查的读取与不带检查的一致。"

#. §0: `simp [lookupChecked, lookupRaw, List.getD, List.getElem?_eq_getElem h]`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:45
msgid "Unfold both definitions and use the in-range assumption to evaluate the indexing:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "把两个定义都展开，并用「在范围内」这条假设把取下标求值出来：\n"
"§0。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L01_TheSameAnswerWhereItMatters.lean:49
msgid "On its domain, the replacement computes what the original computed.\n"
"\n"
"Say exactly that and no more. The theorem does not claim the two functions are the same — they\n"
"are not, and could not be, since one of them can report failure. It claims that a caller who\n"
"only ever passes in-range indices cannot tell them apart.\n"
"\n"
"That qualified form is what *equivalence* almost always means in practice, and the next level\n"
"is about the part the qualification leaves out."
msgstr "在它的定义域上，替换者算出的正是原来那个所算出的。\n"
"\n"
"就说这么多，不要多说。这个定理并没有论断两个函数相同——它们不相同，也不可能相同，\n"
"因为其中一个能报告失败。它论断的是：一个只会传入范围内下标的调用方，分辨不出它们。\n"
"\n"
"这种带限定的形式，几乎就是实践中*等价*一词的含义，而下一关讲的是这份限定所留在外面的那部分。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:8
msgid "Safety Is a Different Claim"
msgstr "安全性是另一回事"

#. §0: `none`
#. §1: `none`
#. §2: `lookupRaw`
#. §3: `lookupRaw`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:10
msgid "Level 1 said the checked lookup behaves like the raw one **where the raw one is meaningful**.\n"
"It said nothing at all about the other indices — and the other indices are the reason anyone\n"
"would make the change.\n"
"\n"
"So here is the second claim, and it is independent of the first: out of range, the checked\n"
"lookup returns §0. It does not invent a value, and it does not return something a caller\n"
"could mistake for data.\n"
"\n"
"Two separate properties, and it is worth being precise about why they cannot be merged.\n"
"*Behavior preservation under a precondition* is about agreeing with the thing you replaced.\n"
"*Safety* is about what you do where the thing you replaced had nothing sensible to do. A\n"
"replacement can have the first without the second, and the second without the first.\n"
"\n"
"A caution, since this example is a model of a real situation. In C, reading past the end of an\n"
"array is **undefined behavior**: the program may return a value, may crash, may do something\n"
"the compiler inferred could never happen. It is not an error return that can be compared with\n"
"§1, and §2 is not a model of it. §3 is a total Lean function with a\n"
"documented default, and the theorems here are about that."
msgstr "第一关说的是带检查的读取在**不带检查那个有意义的地方**与它表现一致。\n"
"它对其他那些下标什么也没说——而其他那些下标正是有人要做这次更改的原因。\n"
"\n"
"所以这是第二个论断，它独立于第一个：越界时，带检查的读取返回 §0。\n"
"它不编造一个值，也不返回某种调用方可能误当成数据的东西。\n"
"\n"
"两条分开的性质，而它们为什么不能合并，值得说准确。*前置条件之下的行为保持*讲的是与你所替换掉的\n"
"那个东西保持一致。*安全性*讲的是在你所替换掉的那个东西本来就无事可做的地方你做什么。\n"
"一个替换者可以有前者而无后者，也可以有后者而无前者。\n"
"\n"
"一句提醒，因为这个例子是对一个真实情形的建模。在 C 里，读到数组末尾之外是**未定义行为**：\n"
"程序可能返回一个值，可能崩溃，也可能做出编译器推断永远不会发生的事。它不是一个可以拿来与\n"
"§1 作比较的错误返回，而 §2 也不是它的模型。§3 是一个带有明确默认值的全 Lean 函数，\n"
"而这里的定理讲的是那个。"

#. §0: `lookupChecked_none : xs.length ≤ i → lookupChecked xs i = none`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:32
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Out of range, the checked lookup reports failure rather than inventing a value."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"越界时，带检查的读取报告失败，而不是编造一个值。"

#. §0: `none`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:39
msgid "Show that the checked lookup returns §0 on every out-of-range index."
msgstr "证明带检查的读取在每个越界下标上都返回 §0。"

#. §0: `simp [lookupChecked]`
#. §1: `omega`
#. §2: `«{h}»`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:42
msgid "Unfold the definition: §0. What is left is the arithmetic side\n"
"condition, which §1 discharges from §2."
msgstr "把定义展开：§0。剩下的是那个算术旁条件，由 §1 从 §2 把它了结。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L02_SafetyIsADifferentClaim.lean:47
msgid "The replacement is safe, and that is a different theorem from the replacement being faithful.\n"
"\n"
"Keep the two apart whenever you argue that one component may stand in for another. *It behaves\n"
"the same* and *it fails well* are both worth having, neither implies the other, and conflating\n"
"them is how a migration gets signed off on half the evidence.\n"
"\n"
"From here on the systems have state, the observations are sequences rather than single\n"
"answers, and *behaves the same* needs a much more careful definition."
msgstr "替换者是安全的，而这与「替换者是忠实的」是两个不同的定理。\n"
"\n"
"每当你论证某个组件可以顶替另一个时，都把这两件事分开。*它表现相同*和*它失败得体面*都值得拥有，\n"
"两者谁也不蕴涵谁，而把它们混为一谈，正是一次迁移凭一半证据就被签字放行的来由。\n"
"\n"
"从这里起，系统带有状态，观察结果是序列而不是单个答案，而*表现相同*需要一个仔细得多的定义。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:8
msgid "What an Observer Sees"
msgstr "观察者看到什么"

#. §0: ```
#. def counterSpec : LTS ℕ StackOp where
#.   Tr := fun n op m => match op with
#.     | .push => m = n + 1
#.     | .pop => 0 < n ∧ m = n - 1
#. ```
#. §1: ```
#. def stackImpl : LTS (List Unit) StackOp where
#.   Tr := fun l op l' => match op with
#.     | .push => l' = () :: l
#.     | .pop => ∃ t, l = () :: t ∧ l' = t
#. ```
#. §2: `Cslib.LTS.traces`
#. §3: `implTraces l`
#. §4: `l`
#. §5: `Cslib.LTS.MTr.cons_iff`
#. §6: ```
#. lts.MTr s₁ (μ :: μs) s₃ ↔ ∃ s₂, lts.Tr s₁ μ s₂ ∧ lts.MTr s₂ μs s₃
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:10
msgid "Now two systems with state. The specification is an abstract counter — it only remembers how\n"
"many items are stored:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"The implementation keeps the items in a list:\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"Their states are not the same type, so there is nothing to compare directly. What *can* be\n"
"compared is what an outsider sees: the sequences of operations each system is able to perform.\n"
"That set is §2, and §3 is the notation this game uses for the\n"
"implementation's traces from state §4.\n"
"\n"
"A word is a trace exactly when some execution performs it — so proving membership means\n"
"exhibiting the execution. §5 lets you give it one step at a time:\n"
"\n"
"§6\n"
"\n"
"Show that pushing twice and popping once is something the empty stack can do."
msgstr "现在是两个带状态的系统。规约是一个抽象的计数器——它只记住存了多少件东西：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"实现把这些东西放在一个列表里：\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"它们的状态不是同一个类型，所以没有什么可以直接比较。*可以*比较的是外部看到的东西：\n"
"每个系统有能力执行的操作序列。那个集合是 §2，而 §3 是本游戏用来表示实现从状态 §4\n"
"出发的迹的记号。\n"
"\n"
"一个词是迹，当且仅当某段执行把它走完——所以证明它属于迹集合，意味着把那段执行拿出来。\n"
"§5 让你一步一步地给出它：\n"
"\n"
"§6\n"
"\n"
"表明「压入两次、弹出一次」是空栈做得到的事。"

#. §0: `stack_trace_example : [StackOp.push, StackOp.push, StackOp.pop] ∈ implTraces []`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:46
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"A concrete behavior of the list-based stack, exhibited by the execution that performs it."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"基于列表的栈的一条具体行为，由执行它的那段运行给出。"

#. §0: `push, push, pop`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:53
msgid "Show that §0 is a behavior the empty list-based stack can exhibit."
msgstr "表明 §0 是空的、基于列表的栈能表现出的一条行为。"

#. §0: `traces`
#. §1: `rw [Cslib.LTS.mem_traces_iff]`
#. §2: `refine ⟨[()], ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:56
msgid "Membership in §0 means some execution performs the word.\n"
"§1 turns the goal into that existential, and the state it ends\n"
"in is a one-element stack: §2."
msgstr "属于 §0 意味着某段执行把这个词走完。§1 把目标变成那个存在陈述，\n"
"而它停在的状态是一个单元素的栈：§2。"

#. §0: `rw [Cslib.LTS.MTr.cons_iff]`
#. §1: `[()]`
#. §2: `refine ⟨[()], rfl, ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:61
msgid "Now peel off the steps. §0 asks for the state after the\n"
"first push, which is §1: §2."
msgstr "现在把那些步骤一步步剥下来。§0 问的是第一次压入之后的状态，也就是 §1：§2。"

#. §0: `[(), ()]`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:65
msgid "The second push takes it to §0."
msgstr "第二次压入把它带到 §0。"

#. §0: `[()]`
#. §1: `exact ⟨[()], ⟨[()], rfl, rfl⟩, Cslib.LTS.MTr.refl⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:68
msgid "And the pop takes it back to §0, where the execution stops. A pop needs a witness\n"
"for the tail: §1."
msgstr "而弹出把它带回 §0，执行就在那里停下。一次弹出需要给出尾部的见证：§1。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L03_WhatAnObserverSees.lean:73
msgid "One behavior, and the run that produces it.\n"
"\n"
"The set of all such words is the only thing an observer who can see operations but not states\n"
"has access to, so it is the natural currency for comparing systems whose states are different\n"
"kinds of thing. That is what the next two levels do with it.\n"
"\n"
"One warning about traces, which the end of this world returns to. A trace set records *which*\n"
"sequences are possible and forgets *when* the system committed to them. Two systems can offer\n"
"an observer exactly the same words and still differ in a way that matters."
msgstr "一条行为，以及产生它的那次运行。\n"
"\n"
"所有这类词构成的集合，是一个能看见操作却看不见状态的观察者所能接触到的全部，\n"
"所以它是比较两个状态类型不同的系统时自然的通货。接下来两关就是拿它来做事。\n"
"\n"
"关于迹有一句警告，本世界结尾会回到它。一个迹集合记录的是*哪些*序列是可能的，\n"
"却忘掉了系统是*何时*对它们做出承诺的。两个系统可以提供给观察者完全相同的词，\n"
"却仍然在要紧的地方不同。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:8
msgid "One Step Answered by One Step"
msgstr "一步由一步应答"

#. §0: ```
#. LTS.IsSimulation lts₁ lts₂ r
#.   ↔ ∀ s₁ s₂, r s₁ s₂ → ∀ μ s₁', lts₁.Tr s₁ μ s₁' → ∃ s₂', lts₂.Tr s₂ μ s₂' ∧ r s₁' s₂'
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:10
msgid "Comparing trace sets directly means reasoning about words of arbitrary length — the same\n"
"problem World 3 had with executions, and it has the same solution: find a local condition and\n"
"let a general theorem do the induction.\n"
"\n"
"The local condition is a **simulation**. Relate states of the two systems, and require that\n"
"whenever related states are given and the first takes a step, the second can answer with a\n"
"step on the same label, landing in related states again:\n"
"\n"
"![A step of the implementation answered by a step of the specification](images/en/simulation.svg)\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"For the stack and the counter the relation is the obvious one: a list stands for its length.\n"
"\n"
"Prove that it is a simulation. There are two cases, one per operation, and neither mentions\n"
"words at all — which is the point."
msgstr "直接比较迹集合，意味着要对任意长度的词做推理——这和第三世界在执行上遇到的是同一个问题，\n"
"而它也有同一个解法：找一个局部条件，让一条一般的定理去做归纳。\n"
"\n"
"那个局部条件就是**模拟**。把两个系统的状态关联起来，并要求：只要给定一对相关的状态、\n"
"而第一个迈出一步，第二个就能用同标号的一步来应答，并重新落在一对相关的状态上：\n"
"\n"
"![实现的一步由规约的一步应答](images/zh/simulation.svg)\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"对栈和计数器而言，这个关系是显然的那个：一个列表代表它的长度。\n"
"\n"
"证明它是一个模拟。有两种情形，每个操作一种，而且两者都完全没有提到词——这正是要点。"

#. §0: `stack_sim_counter : LTS.IsSimulation stackImpl counterSpec (fun l n => l.length = n)`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:33
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Relating a list to its length is a simulation of the counter specification by the list-based\n"
"stack."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"把一个列表与它的长度关联起来，是基于列表的栈对计数器规约的一个模拟。"

#. §0: `counterSpec`
#. §1: `stackImpl`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:41
msgid "Show that *a list stands for its length* is a simulation of §0 by\n"
"§1."
msgstr "证明*一个列表代表它的长度*是 §1 对 §0 的一个模拟。"

#. §0: `intro l n hr μ l' htr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:45
msgid "Introduce the related states, the label, the implementation's step, and the evidence\n"
"that it is one: §0."
msgstr "把相关的两个状态、标号、实现的那一步，以及它确实是一步的证据都引入进来：§0。"

#. §0: `«{μ}»`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:48
msgid "Split on the operation §0: a push and a pop are answered differently."
msgstr "就操作 §0 分情况：入栈与出栈的应答方式不同。"

#. §0: `«{n}» + 1`
#. §1: `refine ⟨n + 1, rfl, ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:50
msgid "A push. The specification can always push, so the state it moves to is §0.\n"
"Supply it and the proof that it is a legal step, and leave the relation:\n"
"§1."
msgstr "一次压入。规约总是可以压入，所以它转移到的状态是 §0。把它和「这是合法的一步」的证明供上，\n"
"把关系留下来：§1。"

#. §0: `simp [stackImpl] at htr`
#. §1: `«{l'}»`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:54
msgid "§0 tells you what §1 is, and then the lengths match."
msgstr "§0 告诉你 §1 是什么，然后长度就对上了。"

#. §0: `simp [stackImpl] at htr`
#. §1: `«{l}»`
#. §2: `subst htr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:57
msgid "A pop. §0 tells you exactly what §1 looked like; then\n"
"§2 replaces it."
msgstr "出栈。§0 会原原本本告诉你 §1 长什么样；随后 §2 把它替换掉。"

#. §0: `simp at hr`
#. §1: `«{hr}»`
#. §2: `0 < «{n}»`
#. §3: `exact ⟨n - 1, ⟨by omega, rfl⟩, by omega⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:61
msgid "§0 turns §1 into a statement about lengths. The specification's pop\n"
"needs §2, which now follows by arithmetic — as does the new length.\n"
"§3."
msgstr "§0 把 §1 变成一个关于长度的陈述。规约的弹出需要 §2，\n"
"而它现在由算术推出——新的长度也一样。§3。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L04_OneStepAnsweredByOneStep.lean:67
msgid "A one-step condition, checked on two operations, between systems with different state types.\n"
"\n"
"Notice what the relation had to do. It is not a function from one state space to the other —\n"
"it is a relation, and nothing requires it to be injective or surjective. Many lists stand for\n"
"the same count. That freedom is what makes simulations usable: the implementation may carry\n"
"information the specification does not, as long as every step it takes is one the\n"
"specification permits.\n"
"\n"
"The next level turns this into the statement about behaviors it was built for."
msgstr "一个单步条件，在两个操作上检查了一遍，连接的是两个状态类型不同的系统。\n"
"\n"
"注意这个关系必须做到什么。它不是从一个状态空间到另一个的函数——它是一个关系，\n"
"而且没有什么要求它是单射或满射。很多个列表代表同一个计数。正是这份自由让模拟可用：\n"
"实现可以携带规约所没有的信息，只要它迈出的每一步都是规约所允许的。\n"
"\n"
"下一关把它变成它本来要服务的那个关于行为的陈述。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:8
msgid "An Implementation Refines Its Specification"
msgstr "一个实现精化了它的规约"

#. §0: ```
#. implTraces l ⊆ specTraces n
#. ```
#. §1: `Cslib.LTS.IsSimulation.traces_subset`
#. §2: ```
#. IsSimulation.traces_subset : IsSimulation lts₁ lts₂ r → r s₁ s₂ → lts₁.traces s₁ ⊆ lts₂.traces s₂
#. ```
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:10
msgid "**Refinement** is the claim that every behavior the implementation can exhibit is one the\n"
"specification already permits:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Note the direction, because it is the whole content of the idea. It does **not** say the two\n"
"do the same things. The specification may permit behaviors the implementation never produces,\n"
"and that is not a defect — it is what lets a specification be loose and still be a promise. A\n"
"specification is a bound on behavior, not a description of it.\n"
"\n"
"You have the simulation. §1 turns it into the trace\n"
"inclusion, given that the starting states are related:\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"That theorem contains the induction over words that you did not have to do."
msgstr "**精化**是这样一个论断：实现能表现出的每条行为，都是规约已经允许的：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"注意方向，因为这就是这个想法的全部内容。它**没有**说两者做同样的事情。规约可以允许实现从不产生的\n"
"行为，而这不是缺陷——正是它让一个规约可以宽松，同时仍然是一份承诺。规约是对行为的一个界，\n"
"不是对行为的一份描述。\n"
"\n"
"模拟你已经有了。§1 把它变成迹包含，前提是起始状态是相关的：\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"那条定理里面装着你不必自己做的、对词的归纳。"

#. §0: `stack_refines_counter : l.length = n → implTraces l ⊆ specTraces n`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:34
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Every sequence of operations the list-based stack can perform is one the counter\n"
"specification permits."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"基于列表的栈能执行的每一个操作序列，都是计数器规约所允许的。"

#. §0: `n`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:42
msgid "Show the list-based stack refines the counter specification: when the list has length §0,\n"
"every operation sequence the implementation can perform is permitted by the specification."
msgstr "证明基于列表的栈精化了计数器规约：当列表长度为 §0 时，\n"
"实现能执行的每一个操作序列都为规约所允许。"

#. §0: `Cslib.LTS.IsSimulation.traces_subset`
#. §1: `stack_sim_counter`
#. §2: `«{h}»`
#. §3: `exact stack_sim_counter.traces_subset h`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:46
msgid "The hard part is already a theorem. §0 converts\n"
"§1 into the trace inclusion, given that the starting states are related by\n"
"§2: §3."
msgstr "难的部分已经是一条定理了。§0 把 §1 转成迹包含，前提是起始状态由 §2 关联：§3。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L05_ImplementationRefinesSpec.lean:51
msgid "A refinement between two systems with different state representations, and the only thing you\n"
"reasoned about was a single step.\n"
"\n"
"Three distinctions worth keeping straight, because they are easy to blur and the rest of this\n"
"world takes them apart one at a time:\n"
"\n"
"* **Trace inclusion is one-directional.** The specification here happens to permit exactly the\n"
"  same behaviors, but in general it may permit more.\n"
"* **Simulation implies trace inclusion and is strictly stronger.** It demands a step-by-step\n"
"  correspondence; trace inclusion only compares sets of words. Two systems can have the same\n"
"  traces with no simulation between them, because a trace set forgets *when* a choice was\n"
"  made.\n"
"* **A simulation in one direction says nothing about the other.** Levels 6 and 7 exhibit a\n"
"  pair where one direction holds and the other provably does not.\n"
"\n"
"And a caution that applies to everything in this world. These are statements about the Lean\n"
"models written here, and about nothing else. A proof that this list-based stack refines this\n"
"counter is not a proof about any C or Rust program, and a model in which a bad operation\n"
"simply has no transition says nothing about what a real language does when a program performs\n"
"one."
msgstr "两个状态表示不同的系统之间的一次精化，而你所推理的只有单独一步。\n"
"\n"
"有三个区分值得保持清楚，因为它们很容易被混淆，而本世界余下的部分会一个一个把它们拆开：\n"
"\n"
"* **迹包含是单向的。**这里的规约恰好允许完全相同的行为，但一般而言它可以允许更多。\n"
"* **模拟蕴涵迹包含，而且严格更强。**它要求一步一步的对应；迹包含只比较词的集合。\n"
"  两个系统可以有相同的迹而它们之间没有模拟，因为迹集合忘掉了选择是*何时*做出的。\n"
"* **一个方向上的模拟对另一个方向什么也没说。**第六、第七关给出一对系统，\n"
"  一个方向成立而另一个方向可证地不成立。\n"
"\n"
"还有一句适用于本世界一切内容的提醒。这些都是关于写在这里的 Lean 模型的陈述，不关于别的任何东西。\n"
"「这个基于列表的栈精化这个计数器」的证明，不是关于任何 C 或 Rust 程序的证明；\n"
"而一个「坏操作干脆没有转移」的模型，对真实语言在程序执行这种操作时会做什么只字未言。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:8
msgid "Simulation in One Direction"
msgstr "一个方向上的模拟"

#. §0: `chooseLate`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `b`
#. §3: `c`
#. §4: ```
#. l0 --a--> l1 --b--> l2
#.           l1 --c--> l3
#. ```
#. §5: `chooseEarly`
#. §6: `a`
#. §7: `b`
#. §8: `c`
#. §9: ```
#. e0 --a--> e1 --b--> e2
#. e0 --a--> e3 --c--> e4
#. ```
#. §10: `a`
#. §11: `b`
#. §12: `c`
#. §13: `chooseEarly`
#. §14: `chooseLate`
#. §15: `l1`
#. §16: `e1`
#. §17: `e3`
#. §18: ```
#. def matchEL : Early → Late → Prop
#.   | .e0, .l0 => True   | .e1, .l1 => True   | .e3, .l1 => True
#.   | .e2, .l2 => True   | .e4, .l3 => True
#.   | _, _     => False
#. ```
#. §19: `chooseLate`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:10
msgid "Two systems that offer an observer exactly the same words, and differ in when they decide.\n"
"\n"
"§0 does an §1, and *then* either a §2 or a §3:\n"
"\n"
"§4\n"
"\n"
"§5 has two different §6-steps, one of which has already committed to §7 and the\n"
"other to §8:\n"
"\n"
"§9\n"
"\n"
"An observer sees §10, then §11 or §12, from either. But the systems are not interchangeable,\n"
"and this level and the next show in which direction they fail to be.\n"
"\n"
"Start with the direction that works. Every move §13 makes can be answered by\n"
"§14, because §15 can still do whatever §16 or §17 can. The relation is\n"
"\n"
"§18\n"
"\n"
"Prove it is a simulation. Both systems are finite, so splitting on every state, label and\n"
"target settles most of it outright; the handful of goals that survive are the real steps, and\n"
"each needs the state §19 answers with."
msgstr "两个系统提供给观察者完全相同的词，区别在于它们何时做决定。\n"
"\n"
"§0 先做一个 §1，*然后*做 §2 或 §3 之一：\n"
"\n"
"§4\n"
"\n"
"§5 有两条不同的 §6 步，其中一条已经承诺 §7，另一条已经承诺 §8：\n"
"\n"
"§9\n"
"\n"
"观察者从任一个系统看到的都是 §10，然后是 §11 或 §12。但这两个系统不可互换，\n"
"而本关和下一关会表明它们在哪个方向上不可互换。\n"
"\n"
"从行得通的那个方向开始。§13 所做的每一步都能被 §14 应答，因为 §15 仍然能做\n"
"§16 或 §17 能做的任何事。关系是\n"
"\n"
"§18\n"
"\n"
"证明它是一个模拟。两个系统都是有限的，所以对每个状态、标号和目标做分情形，大部分就直接了结了；\n"
"活下来的那几个目标是真正的步骤，每一个都需要给出 §19 用来应答的那个状态。"

#. §0: `early_sim_late : LTS.IsSimulation chooseEarly chooseLate matchEL`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:47
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The system that chooses early is simulated by the one that chooses late."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"早做选择的那个系统被晚做选择的那个所模拟。"

#. §0: `matchEL`
#. §1: `chooseLate`
#. §2: `chooseEarly`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:54
msgid "Show that §0 is a simulation of §1 by §2."
msgstr "证明 §0 是 §2 对 §1 的一个模拟。"

#. §0: `intro e l hr μ e' htr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:56
msgid "Introduce the related states, the label and the step: §0."
msgstr "把相关的两个状态、标号和那一步引入进来：§0。"

#. §0: `simp_all`
#. §1: `cases e <;> cases l <;> cases μ <;> cases e' <;> simp_all [chooseEarly, chooseLate, matchEL]`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:58
msgid "Both state spaces are finite, so split on all four and let §0 discard every\n"
"combination that is not a real transition of a related pair:\n"
"§1."
msgstr "两个状态空间都是有限的，所以对这四样都做分情形，让 §0 把每个「不是一对相关状态的真实转移」的\n"
"组合都丢掉：§1。"

#. §0: `e0 -a→ e1`
#. §1: `l0 -a→ l1`
#. §2: `trivial`
#. §3: `refine ⟨Late.l1, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> trivial`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:63
msgid "§0, answered by §1. Name the answering state and let §2\n"
"discharge both the transition and the relation:\n"
"§3."
msgstr "§0，由 §1 应答。把用来应答的那个状态命名出来，再让 §2\n"
"把转移和关系两边都了结：\n"
"§3。"

#. §0: `e0 -a→ e3`
#. §1: `l0 -a→ l1`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:67
msgid "§0, answered by the same step §1 — which is exactly why this\n"
"direction works."
msgstr "§0，由同一步 §1 应答——而这恰恰就是这个方向行得通的原因。"

#. §0: `e1 -b→ e2`
#. §1: `l1 -b→ l2`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:70
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:72
msgid "§0, answered by §1."
msgstr "§0，由 §1 应答。"

#. §0: `chooseEarly`
#. §1: `chooseLate`
#. §2: `traces_subset`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `e1`
#. §5: `e3`
#. §6: `l1`
#. §7: `l1`
#. §8: `l1`
#. §9: `chooseEarly`
#. §10: `e1`
#. §11: `e3`
#. §12: `l1`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L06_SimulationInOneDirection.lean:75
msgid "§0 is simulated by §1, so by §2 every behavior of the early\n"
"chooser is a behavior of the late one.\n"
"\n"
"Look at where the two §3-steps went. Both §4 and §5 were answered by the *same* state\n"
"§6, because §7 has kept both options open and can therefore match either commitment. A\n"
"simulation is allowed to be many-to-one like that.\n"
"\n"
"Which should make you suspicious about the other direction, where the single state §8 would\n"
"have to be matched by a single state of §9 — and neither §10 nor §11 can do\n"
"everything §12 can."
msgstr "§0 被 §1 所模拟，所以由 §2，早做选择者的每条行为都是晚做选择者的一条行为。\n"
"\n"
"看看那两条 §3 步去了哪里。§4 和 §5 都被*同一个*状态 §6 应答，\n"
"因为 §7 把两个选项都留着，因而能匹配任何一种承诺。模拟是允许这样多对一的。\n"
"\n"
"而这该让你对另一个方向起疑：在那边，单个状态 §8 得被 §9 的单个状态匹配——\n"
"而 §10 和 §11 谁也做不到 §12 能做的一切。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:8
msgid "And Not the Other"
msgstr "而另一个方向不行"

#. §0: `Cslib.LTS.Similarity lts₁ lts₂ s₁ s₂`
#. §1: `s₁`
#. §2: `s₂`
#. §3: `r`
#. §4: `l0`
#. §5: `e0`
#. §6: `l0 -a→ l1`
#. §7: `r`
#. §8: `l1`
#. §9: `e1`
#. §10: `e3`
#. §11: `l1`
#. §12: `b`
#. §13: `c`
#. §14: `e1`
#. §15: `b`
#. §16: `e3`
#. §17: `c`
#. §18: `r`
#. §19: `rintro ⟨r, hr, hsim⟩`
#. §20: `hsim`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:10
msgid "Now show that there is **no** simulation the other way.\n"
"\n"
"§0 says *some* simulation relates §1 to §2. Refuting\n"
"it means refuting all of them at once, so you do not get to pick the relation — you are handed\n"
"one and must find its contradiction.\n"
"\n"
"The argument is the one the last level's conclusion anticipated. Suppose some simulation §3\n"
"relates §4 to §5. Then §6 must be answered, so §7 relates §8 to one of §9 or\n"
"§10. But §11 can do §12 **and** §13, while §14 can only do §15 and §16 can only do §17. In\n"
"either case §18 is obliged to answer a step that its partner cannot take.\n"
"\n"
"§19 takes the supposed simulation apart. Applying §20 to a step produces\n"
"the answering state, which you then split on."
msgstr "现在表明反方向上**没有**模拟。\n"
"\n"
"§0 说*存在某个*模拟把 §1 与 §2 关联起来。要否证它，就得一次否证所有的模拟，\n"
"所以你没得挑那个关系——别人把一个交给你，而你必须找出它的矛盾。\n"
"\n"
"论证就是上一关结语所预告的那个。假设某个模拟 §3 把 §4 与 §5 关联起来。那么 §6 必须被应答，\n"
"所以 §7 把 §8 与 §9 或 §10 之一关联起来。但 §11 既能做 §12 **又**能做 §13，\n"
"而 §14 只能做 §15，§16 只能做 §17。两种情形下 §18 都被迫去应答一步，\n"
"而它的伙伴迈不出那一步。\n"
"\n"
"§19 把那个假想的模拟拆开。把 §20 用到一步上会产出那个应答的状态，接着你对它做分情形。"

#. §0: `late_not_sim_early : ¬LTS.Similarity chooseLate chooseEarly Late.l0 Early.e0`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:27
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"No simulation relates the late chooser to the early one: simulation is genuinely\n"
"directional."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"没有模拟把晚做选择者与早做选择者关联起来：模拟确实是有方向的。"

#. §0: `chooseLate`
#. §1: `chooseEarly`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:35
msgid "Show that no simulation relates §0's initial state to §1's, so the\n"
"simulation of the previous level has no converse."
msgstr "证明没有模拟把 §0 的初始状态与 §1 的初始状态关联起来，所以上一关的模拟没有逆命题。"

#. §0: `rintro ⟨r, hr, hsim⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:39
msgid "Assume one exists and name its parts: §0."
msgstr "假设存在一个，并给它的各部分命名：§0。"

#. §0: `l0 -a→ l1`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨e', htr, hr'⟩ := hsim hr Act.a Late.l1 (by trivial)`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:41
msgid "The step §0 has to be answered. Ask the simulation for the answer:\n"
"§1."
msgstr "那一步 §0 必须被应答。向模拟索要这个应答：§1。"

#. §0: `«{e'}»`
#. §1: `cases e'`
#. §2: `a`
#. §3: `e0`
#. §4: `l1`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:44
msgid "Now split on which state §0 is: §1. Three of the five cannot be reached by\n"
"an §2 from §3 at all; the other two each lack one of §4's continuations. Take the five\n"
"goals in constructor order with focus dots."
msgstr "现在对 §0 是哪个状态做分情形：§1。五个里有三个根本不可能由从 §3 出发的 §2 抵达；\n"
"另外两个各自缺少 §4 的一条后续。用聚焦点按构造子顺序取这五个目标。"

#. §0: `e0`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `e0`
#. §3: `e0`
#. §4: `«{htr}»`
#. §5: `simp [chooseEarly] at htr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:48
msgid "§0. There is no §1-transition from §2 to §3, so §4 is already false:\n"
"§5."
msgstr "§0。从 §2 到 §3 没有 §1 转移，所以 §4 本身就是假的：§5。"

#. §0: `e1`
#. §1: `b`
#. §2: `c`
#. §3: `l1 -c→ l3`
#. §4: `obtain ⟨ec, htrc, _⟩ := hsim hr' Act.c Late.l3 (by trivial)`
#. §5: `cases ec <;> simp [chooseEarly] at htrc`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:51
msgid "§0 can do §1 but not §2. Ask the simulation to answer §3 and there is\n"
"nowhere for it to go: §4, then\n"
"§5."
msgstr "§0 能做 §1 但不能做 §2。让模拟去应答 §3，它无处可去：§4，然后 §5。"

#. §0: `e2`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `e0`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:56
msgid "§0 is not reachable by an §1 from §2 either."
msgstr "§0 同样不是从 §2 出发经一个 §1 可达的。"

#. §0: `e3`
#. §1: `c`
#. §2: `b`
#. §3: `e1`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:58
msgid "§0 can do §1 but not §2. The mirror image of the §3 case."
msgstr "§0 能做 §1 但不能做 §2。§3 那一情形的镜像。"

#. §0: `e4`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:61
msgid "Nor §0."
msgstr "§0 也不行。"

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `chooseEarly`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `b`
#. §5: `c`
#. §6: `chooseLate`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L07_AndNotTheOther.lean:64
msgid "One direction holds, the other is impossible. Similarity is not symmetric, and a one-way\n"
"simulation is not evidence that two systems are interchangeable.\n"
"\n"
"This is the fact behind the warning in Level 5. If you prove §0 is simulated by §1 and\n"
"conclude *A and B behave the same*, you have asserted something you did not prove, and\n"
"sometimes something false.\n"
"\n"
"What makes the two systems differ is not *which* words they can produce — those sets are\n"
"identical — but *when* they commit. An observer who may interact rather than merely watch can\n"
"tell them apart: offer §2 an §3 and then insist on §4, and it may already have\n"
"chosen §5 and be stuck. §6 never is.\n"
"\n"
"The relation that rules this out is **bisimulation**, and the next level builds one."
msgstr "一个方向成立，另一个不可能。相似性不是对称的，而一个单向的模拟不是两个系统可互换的证据。\n"
"\n"
"这就是第五关那句警告背后的事实。如果你证明了 §0 被 §1 所模拟，就下结论说*A 与 B 表现相同*，\n"
"那你断言了你没有证明的东西，有时还是错的东西。\n"
"\n"
"让这两个系统不同的，不是它们能产生*哪些*词——那两个集合是一样的——而是它们*何时*做承诺。\n"
"一个能交互而不只是旁观的观察者分辨得出来：给 §2 一个 §3，然后坚持要 §4，\n"
"而它可能已经选了 §5 从而卡住。§6 则从不会。\n"
"\n"
"排除掉这种情况的关系是**双模拟**，而下一关搭一个出来。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:8
msgid "Bisimulation Across Representations"
msgstr "跨表示的双模拟"

#. §0: ```
#. LTS.IsBisimulation lts₁ lts₂ r ↔ ∀ s₁ s₂, r s₁ s₂ → ∀ μ,
#.   (∀ s₁', lts₁.Tr s₁ μ s₁' → ∃ s₂', lts₂.Tr s₂ μ s₂' ∧ r s₁' s₂')
#.   ∧
#.   (∀ s₂', lts₂.Tr s₂ μ s₂' → ∃ s₁', lts₁.Tr s₁ μ s₁' ∧ r s₁' s₂')
#. ```
#. §1: `0 < n`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:10
msgid "A **bisimulation** is a single relation that works in both directions at once:\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Note that it is not *a simulation whose converse is also a simulation* — it is one relation\n"
"required to answer challenges from both sides. That is strictly stronger than mutual\n"
"simulation by two unrelated relations, and it is the right notion of *these two systems are\n"
"interchangeable*.\n"
"\n"
"Go back to the stack and the counter. In Level 4 you showed that a list standing for its\n"
"length simulates. Show now that the **same relation** is a bisimulation: not only can the\n"
"specification answer the implementation, the implementation can answer the specification.\n"
"\n"
"The new half is the pop. The specification's pop requires only §1. To answer it the\n"
"implementation must produce an actual list to pop, so you have to get from *the length is\n"
"positive* to *the list is non-empty* — which means splitting on the list."
msgstr "**双模拟**是一个同时在两个方向上都奏效的单一关系：\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"注意它不是*一个逆也是模拟的模拟*——它是一个被要求应答两边挑战的关系。\n"
"这严格强于由两个互不相干的关系给出的相互模拟，而它才是*这两个系统可互换*的正确概念。\n"
"\n"
"回到栈和计数器。第四关里你表明了「列表代表它的长度」构成一个模拟。现在表明**同一个关系**\n"
"是一个双模拟：不仅规约能应答实现，实现也能应答规约。\n"
"\n"
"新的那一半是弹出。规约的弹出只要求 §1。要应答它，实现必须拿出一个真实的列表来弹，\n"
"所以你得从*长度为正*走到*列表非空*——这意味着对列表做分情形。"

#. §0: `stack_bisim_counter : LTS.IsBisimulation stackImpl counterSpec (fun l n => l.length = n)`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:35
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The list-based stack and the counter specification are bisimilar under the relation that a\n"
"list stands for its length."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"在「一个列表代表它的长度」这个关系之下，基于列表的栈与计数器规约是双模拟的。"

#. §0: `stackImpl`
#. §1: `counterSpec`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:43
msgid "Show that *a list stands for its length* is a bisimulation between §0 and\n"
"§1."
msgstr "证明*一个列表代表它的长度*是 §0 与 §1 之间的一个双模拟。"

#. §0: `intro l n hr μ`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:47
msgid "Introduce the related states and the label: §0."
msgstr "把相关的两个状态和标号引入进来：§0。"

#. §0: `refine ⟨fun l' htr => stack_sim_counter hr μ l' htr, ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:49
msgid "The first half is exactly the simulation you already proved. Supply it and keep the\n"
"second: §0."
msgstr "前一半恰好就是你已经证过的那个模拟。把它供上，留下后一半：§0。"

#. §0: `intro n' htr`
#. §1: `cases μ`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:52
msgid "Now the new direction: the specification steps, and the implementation must answer.\n"
"§0, then §1."
msgstr "现在是新的方向：规约迈出一步，而实现必须应答。先 §0，再 §1。"

#. §0: `() :: «{l}»`
#. §1: `refine ⟨() :: l, rfl, ?_⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:56
msgid "A push. The implementation can always push, producing §0:\n"
"§1, and then the lengths match."
msgstr "一次压入。实现总是可以压入，产出 §0：§1，然后长度就对上了。"

#. §0: `simp [counterSpec] at htr`
#. §1: `0 < «{n}»`
#. §2: `obtain ⟨hpos, rfl⟩ := htr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:61
msgid "A pop. §0 gives you §1 and what the new count is;\n"
"§2 names them."
msgstr "一次弹出。§0 给你 §1 以及新的计数是什么；§2 把它们命名。"

#. §0: `cases l with`
#. §1: `«{hr}»`
#. §2: `«{hpos}»`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:65
msgid "To answer, the implementation needs a non-empty list. Split: §0. The\n"
"empty case contradicts §1 together with §2, and the non-empty case supplies the\n"
"tail."
msgstr "要应答，实现需要一个非空的列表。拆开：§0。空的那种情形与 §1 连同 §2 矛盾，\n"
"而非空的那种给出尾部。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L08_BisimulationAcrossRepresentations.lean:72
msgid "The stack and the counter are bisimilar. Neither can be distinguished from the other by any\n"
"observer, however it interacts.\n"
"\n"
"That is a much stronger statement than the refinement of Level 5, and it is the one you would\n"
"want before replacing a component in a system you do not control. Refinement promises the\n"
"replacement does nothing the specification forbids. Bisimulation promises it does nothing\n"
"different at all.\n"
"\n"
"Both were proved from a local, one-step condition, over states that are not even the same\n"
"type. The list carries strictly more information than the count — the identity of the items —\n"
"and the relation simply ignores it. That is the sense in which the counter is an *abstraction*\n"
"of the stack, and it is the same idea you met in World 1, now between two systems rather than\n"
"between a machine and a program."
msgstr "栈与计数器是双模拟的。任何观察者，不论如何交互，都无法把其中一个与另一个区分开。\n"
"\n"
"这比第五关的精化强得多，而且正是你在替换一个你无法掌控的系统里的组件之前会想要的那个。\n"
"精化承诺的是替换者不做规约所禁止的事。双模拟承诺的是它根本不做任何不同的事。\n"
"\n"
"两者都是从一个局部的单步条件证出来的，而所涉的状态连类型都不相同。列表携带的信息严格多于计数——\n"
"那些东西各自的身份——而关系干脆忽略它。正是在这个意义上计数器是栈的一个*抽象*，\n"
"而这与你在第一世界遇到的是同一个想法，只是现在发生在两个系统之间，而不是机器与程序之间。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:8
msgid "A Step Nobody Can See"
msgstr "一个谁也看不见的步骤"

#. §0: `Cslib.HasTau`
#. §1: ```
#. delayed:  d0 --τ--> d1 --out--> d2
#. direct:   n0 --out--> n1
#. ```
#. §2: `d0`
#. §3: `τ`
#. §4: `n0`
#. §5: `τ`
#. §6: `τ`
#. §7: `τ`
#. §8: `IsSWBisimulation`
#. §9: `STr`
#. §10: ```
#. LTS.STr.refl   : lts.STr s τ s                     -- answer a τ by standing still
#. LTS.STr.single : lts.Tr s μ s' → lts.STr s μ s'    -- answer a visible step directly
#. ```
#. §11: `matchDN`
#. §12: `d0`
#. §13: `d1`
#. §14: `n0`
#. §15: `n0 -out→ n1`
#. §16: `d0`
#. §17: `out`
#. §18: `τ`
#. §19: `d1`
#. §20: `out`
#. §21: `delayed_out_step`
#. §22: `LTS.STr.tr`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:10
msgid "Real implementations do work that is not part of their interface: a cache lookup, a\n"
"reallocation, a bookkeeping update. Those steps are real, and an observer at the interface\n"
"cannot see them.\n"
"\n"
"CSlib marks one label as internal with the class §0. The implementation here does\n"
"one invisible step before it produces its output; the specification produces the output\n"
"straight away:\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"They are **not** bisimilar in the strict sense of Level 8: §2 can take a §3-step and §4\n"
"cannot match it with a §5-step of its own. Under a notion of equivalence that counts\n"
"invisible work, every piece of internal bookkeeping would make an implementation inequivalent\n"
"to its specification, which is useless.\n"
"\n"
"**Weak bisimilarity** is the repair. A challenge must still be answered, but the answer may be\n"
"padded with any number of §6-steps before and after — and a §7-challenge may be answered by\n"
"doing nothing at all. CSlib's convenient formulation is §8, where the challenge\n"
"is a single transition and the answer is a *saturated* transition §9:\n"
"\n"
"§10\n"
"\n"
"The relation is §11, which maps both §12 and §13 to §14, precisely because the step\n"
"between them cannot be seen.\n"
"\n"
"For the challenge §15, the implementation must answer from §16 with a saturated\n"
"§17-transition: a §18 to §19, then the real §20. That composite is §21,\n"
"built for you from §22."
msgstr "真实的实现会做一些不属于其接口的工作：一次缓存查找、一次重新分配、一次记账更新。\n"
"那些步骤是真实的，而接口处的观察者看不见它们。\n"
"\n"
"CSlib 用类 §0 把一个标号标记为内部的。这里的实现在产出输出之前做一步不可见的工作；\n"
"规约则直接产出输出：\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"按第八关那种严格意义，它们**不是**双模拟的：§2 能迈出一步 §3，而 §4 没法用自己的一步 §5 来匹配。\n"
"在一个把不可见工作也算进去的等价概念之下，每一点内部记账都会让实现与它的规约不等价，\n"
"那是没用的。\n"
"\n"
"**弱双模拟**是这个修补。挑战仍然必须被应答，但应答前后可以垫上任意多的 §6 步——\n"
"而一个 §7 挑战可以用什么都不做来应答。CSlib 便于使用的表述是 §8，\n"
"其中挑战是单独一个转移，而应答是一个*饱和*转移 §9：\n"
"\n"
"§10\n"
"\n"
"关系是 §11，它把 §12 和 §13 都映到 §14，恰恰因为它们之间那一步看不见。\n"
"\n"
"对挑战 §15，实现必须从 §16 用一个饱和的 §17 转移来应答：先一个 §18 到 §19，\n"
"再是真正的 §20。那个复合步骤是 §21，已经用 §22 为你搭好了。"

#. §0: `delayed_sw_direct : LTS.IsSWBisimulation delayed direct matchDN`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:48
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"The implementation with an internal step and the specification without one answer each\n"
"other's visible challenges, up to invisible work."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"带一步内部工作的实现与不带内部工作的规约，在容许不可见工作的意义下互相应答对方的可见挑战。"

#. §0: `matchDN`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:56
msgid "Show that §0 is a weak bisimulation (in CSlib's single-challenge form) between the\n"
"implementation that does internal work and the specification that does not."
msgstr "证明 §0 是那个做内部工作的实现与那个不做内部工作的规约之间的一个弱双模拟（用 CSlib 的单挑战形式）。"

#. §0: `intro d n hr μ`
#. §1: `constructor`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:59
msgid "Introduce the related states and the label, then split the two directions:\n"
"§0, then §1."
msgstr "把相关的两个状态和标号引入进来，然后把两个方向分开：先 §0，再 §1。"

#. §0: `intro d' htr`
#. §1: `simp_all`
#. §2: `cases d <;> cases n <;> cases μ <;> cases d' <;> simp_all [delayed, direct, matchDN]`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:63
msgid "The implementation challenges. §0, then split on everything and let\n"
"§1 discard the impossible combinations:\n"
"§2."
msgstr "实现发起挑战。先 §0，然后对一切做分情形，让 §1 把不可能的组合丢掉：§2。"

#. §0: `d0 -τ→ d1`
#. §1: `STr.refl`
#. §2: `d1`
#. §3: `n0`
#. §4: `refine ⟨Direct.n0, Cslib.LTS.STr.refl, ?_⟩`
#. §5: `trivial`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:69
msgid "§0. The specification answers by standing still — §1 — and §2\n"
"still stands for §3: §4, then §5."
msgstr "§0。规约用原地不动来应答——§1——而 §2 仍然代表 §3：先 §4，再 §5。"

#. §0: `d1 -out→ d2`
#. §1: `out`
#. §2: `refine ⟨Direct.n1, Cslib.LTS.STr.single (by trivial), ?_⟩`
#. §3: `trivial`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:73
msgid "§0, answered by the specification's own §1:\n"
"§2, then §3."
msgstr "§0，由规约自己的 §1 应答：先 §2，再 §3。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:77
msgid "Now the specification challenges, and the implementation must answer."
msgstr "现在轮到规约发起挑战，而实现必须应答。"

#. §0: `d0`
#. §1: `out`
#. §2: `delayed_out_step`
#. §3: `refine ⟨Delayed.d2, delayed_out_step, ?_⟩`
#. §4: `trivial`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:81
msgid "From §0, answering §1 requires doing the invisible step first. That composite\n"
"is §2: §3, then §4."
msgstr "从 §0 出发，要应答 §1 就得先做那步不可见的。那个复合步骤是 §2：先 §3，再 §4。"

#. §0: `d1`
#. §1: `out`
#. §2: `refine ⟨Delayed.d2, Cslib.LTS.STr.single (by trivial), ?_⟩`
#. §3: `trivial`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:85
msgid "From §0 the §1 is immediate:\n"
"§2, then §3."
msgstr "从 §0 出发 §1 是立刻的：先 §2，再 §3。"

#. §0: `d0 ≈ n0`
#. §1: `IsSWBisimulation.isWeakBisimulation`
#. §2: `τ`
#. §3: `Divergence`
#. §4: `Termination`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L09_AStepNobodyCanSee.lean:90
msgid "The implementation and the specification are weakly bisimilar: §0, via\n"
"§1.\n"
"\n"
"Weak bisimilarity is what you usually want when comparing an implementation with a\n"
"specification, because specifications are written without the implementation's bookkeeping and\n"
"should not have to anticipate it. The cost of the weakening is real, though, and worth\n"
"knowing: weak bisimilarity cannot see how *much* internal work is done, so a system that\n"
"diverges — spinning on §2 forever and never producing the output — is weakly bisimilar to one\n"
"that produces it immediately. If termination matters, weak bisimilarity is not the relation\n"
"that establishes it, and CSlib's §3 and §4 are where to look instead.\n"
"\n"
"One relation left to discuss, which is the one you have been using all along without being\n"
"asked to choose it."
msgstr "实现与规约是弱双模拟的：§0，经由 §1。\n"
"\n"
"在把一个实现与一个规约作比较时，你通常想要的就是弱双模拟，因为规约是在不考虑实现的记账的情况下\n"
"写出来的，也不该被要求去预见那些记账。不过这次弱化的代价是真实的，而且值得知道：\n"
"弱双模拟看不出内部工作做了*多少*，所以一个发散的系统——永远在 §2 上空转、从不产出输出——\n"
"与一个立刻产出输出的系统是弱双模拟的。如果终止性要紧，弱双模拟不是确立它的那个关系，\n"
"而 CSlib 的 §3 与 §4 才是该去看的地方。\n"
"\n"
"还剩一个关系要讨论，而它正是你一路在用、却从没被要求去挑选的那个。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:8
msgid "Choosing the Right Relation"
msgstr "挑对关系"

#. §0: `l ~tr[stackImpl, counterSpec] n`
#. §1: `IsBisimulation.traceEq`
#. §2: `chooseLate`
#. §3: `chooseEarly`
#. §4: `IsBisimulation.isSimulation`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:10
msgid "Every level so far told you which relation to prove. This one does not; it tells you what you\n"
"need to know about two pairs of systems, and leaves you to notice that the answers come from\n"
"different places.\n"
"\n"
"**First.** A caller of the stack wants to know it cannot tell the stack from the counter —\n"
"that they are **trace equivalent**, §0. You could try to compute\n"
"both trace sets and compare them. You should not: you proved a bisimulation in Level 8, and\n"
"§1 says bisimilar states have the same traces. Picking the strong\n"
"relation first made the weak one free.\n"
"\n"
"**Second.** Someone proposes replacing §2 with §3, on the grounds that\n"
"they have the same traces — which they do. Show that they are nevertheless **not bisimilar**.\n"
"You do not need a new argument: a bisimulation is in particular a simulation, via\n"
"§4, and Level 7 showed there is no simulation in that direction.\n"
"\n"
"Together these are the shape of the whole world. Trace equivalence is what an observer who\n"
"only watches can detect. Bisimilarity is what an observer who interacts can detect. They are\n"
"different, bisimilarity is strictly stronger, and which one you need is a question about your\n"
"setting — not about Lean."
msgstr "到目前为止每一关都告诉你要证明哪个关系。这一关不告诉你；它告诉你关于两对系统你需要知道什么，\n"
"然后留给你自己去注意：答案来自不同的地方。\n"
"\n"
"**第一对。**栈的一个调用方想知道它分辨不出栈和计数器——也就是它们**迹等价**，§0。\n"
"你可以试着把两个迹集合都算出来再比较。你不该这么做：你在第八关证明了一个双模拟，\n"
"而 §1 说双模拟的状态有相同的迹。先挑那个强的关系，弱的就白得了。\n"
"\n"
"**第二对。**有人提议用 §3 替换 §2，理由是它们有相同的迹——它们确实有。\n"
"请表明它们仍然**不是双模拟的**。你不需要新的论证：双模拟特别地也是一个模拟，经由 §4，\n"
"而第七关表明那个方向上没有模拟。\n"
"\n"
"合起来，这两对就是整个世界的形状。迹等价是一个只旁观的观察者能察觉的东西。\n"
"双模拟是一个会交互的观察者能察觉的东西。它们不同，双模拟严格更强，而你需要哪一个，\n"
"是一个关于你所处场景的问题——不是关于 Lean 的问题。"

#. §0: `relation_choice`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:33
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"Bisimilarity gives trace equivalence for free; trace equivalence does not give bisimilarity."
msgstr "§0\n"
"\n"
"双模拟白送你迹等价；迹等价不送你双模拟。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:40
msgid "Establish both halves of the comparison: the stack and the counter are trace equivalent,\n"
"and the two choice systems are not bisimilar even though they are."
msgstr "把比较的两半都确立起来：栈与计数器迹等价；而那两个选择系统尽管迹等价，却不是双模拟的。"

#. §0: `constructor`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:46
msgid "Two independent claims. §0 splits them."
msgstr "两个互相独立的论断。§0 把它们拆开。"

#. §0: `IsBisimulation.traceEq`
#. §1: `intro l n h`
#. §2: `exact stack_bisim_counter.traceEq h`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:48
msgid "Introduce the states and the relating equation, then hand the bisimulation to\n"
"§0: §1, then §2."
msgstr "把状态和那条关联等式引入进来，再把双模拟交给 §0：先 §1，再 §2。"

#. §0: `rintro ⟨r, hr, hb⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:52
msgid "Assume a bisimulation and take it apart: §0."
msgstr "假设有一个双模拟并把它拆开：§0。"

#. §0: `exact late_not_sim_early ⟨r, hr, hb.isSimulation⟩`
#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:54
msgid "A bisimulation is a simulation, and Level 7 ruled those out:\n"
"§0."
msgstr "双模拟是一个模拟，而第七关已经把那些排除掉了：§0。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement/L10_ChoosingTheRightRelation.lean:58
msgid "Four relations, and the discipline for choosing between them.\n"
"\n"
"* **Conditional functional equivalence.** The replacement computes the same answers, on the\n"
"  inputs where the original was meaningful. Say which inputs.\n"
"* **Trace inclusion — refinement.** Every behavior of the implementation is permitted by the\n"
"  specification. One-directional, and that asymmetry is a feature.\n"
"* **Simulation.** A local condition implying trace inclusion, and strictly stronger than it.\n"
"  A simulation one way says nothing about the other.\n"
"* **Bisimulation.** One relation answering challenges from both sides. Implies trace\n"
"  equivalence, and is implied by it only under extra assumptions such as determinism. Weakened\n"
"  to ignore internal steps, it is the usual notion of *this implementation realises this\n"
"  specification*.\n"
"\n"
"The habit to carry away is to ask what an observer of your system can actually do before\n"
"choosing. If they only read a log, trace equivalence is what you need and anything stronger is\n"
"work you did not have to do. If they can interact — hold a handle, make a request and insist\n"
"on a response — trace equivalence is not enough, and proving it would be proving something true\n"
"that does not mean what you wanted.\n"
"\n"
"And the caveat from Level 5 one last time, because it is the easiest thing in this world to\n"
"overclaim. Everything here is about the Lean models on this page. A relation between two\n"
"models is evidence about two programs only to the extent that the models are faithful, and\n"
"establishing *that* is a different kind of work than anything this game has asked you to do."
msgstr "四个关系，以及在它们之间做选择的规矩。\n"
"\n"
"* **条件函数等价。**在原来那个有意义的那些输入上，替换者算出相同的答案。要说清是哪些输入。\n"
"* **迹包含——精化。**实现的每条行为都被规约所允许。单向的，而这份不对称是一个特性。\n"
"* **模拟。**一个蕴涵迹包含、并且严格强于它的局部条件。一个方向上的模拟对另一个方向什么也没说。\n"
"* **双模拟。**一个应答两边挑战的关系。它蕴涵迹等价，而只有在额外假设（例如确定性）之下才被迹等价\n"
"  所蕴涵。把它弱化成忽略内部步骤，就是*这个实现实现了这个规约*的通常含义。\n"
"\n"
"要带走的习惯是：在挑选之前，先问你系统的观察者实际上能做什么。如果他们只读日志，\n"
"那迹等价就是你需要的，任何更强的都是你本不必做的工作。如果他们能交互——\n"
"握着一个句柄，发出一个请求并坚持要一个响应——那迹等价就不够，而证明它就会是\n"
"证明了一件为真、却不是你本来想说的事。\n"
"\n"
"还有第五关那条告诫，最后再说一遍，因为它是本世界里最容易说过头的东西。这里的一切都是关于本页上的\n"
"Lean 模型的。两个模型之间的一个关系，只在模型忠实的限度内才是关于两个程序的证据，\n"
"而确立*那件事*，是一种与本游戏所要求过的任何事情都不同的工作。"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement.lean:4
msgid "Refinement and Behavioral Equivalence"
msgstr "精化与行为等价"

#: Game/Levels/Refinement.lean:6
msgid "*Optional branch.* You can finish the core path without this world, and nothing later depends\n"
"on it. It is here because the question it asks comes up constantly in practice: **may I\n"
"replace this component with that one?**\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes the honest answer is *yes, they compute the same thing* — but only on inputs that\n"
"satisfy some condition. Sometimes it is *the replacement is safer, and that is a different\n"
"claim from behaving the same*. Sometimes the two systems do not even have the same notion of\n"
"state, and the only thing you can compare is what an outside observer sees. And sometimes the\n"
"implementation does internal work that no observer can see at all, and the right notion of\n"
"equivalence has to ignore it.\n"
"\n"
"So this world is about choosing the right relation: conditional equivalence, trace inclusion,\n"
"one-way simulation, bisimulation, and weak bisimulation. They are not interchangeable, and\n"
"picking the wrong one is how people end up proving something true that does not mean what they\n"
"wanted. You will see a pair of systems that are related in one direction and provably not in\n"
"the other, and a pair that offer an observer identical behavior and are still not\n"
"interchangeable.\n"
"\n"
"A caution before you start. These are statements about the Lean models written here, and about\n"
"nothing else. A proof that this list-based stack refines this counter is not a proof about any\n"
"C or Rust program, and a model in which a bad operation simply has no transition says nothing\n"
"about what a real language does when a program performs one."
msgstr "*可选分支。*没有本世界你也能走完核心路线，而且后面没有任何内容依赖它。它在这里，\n"
"是因为它所问的问题在实践中不断出现：**我可以拿那个组件替换这个吗？**\n"
"\n"
"有时诚实的答案是*可以，它们算出同样的东西*——但只在满足某个条件的输入上。有时答案是\n"
"*替换者更安全，而这与表现相同是不同的论断*。有时两个系统连状态的概念都不相同，\n"
"唯一可比的只有外部观察者看到的东西。还有时实现做的内部工作观察者根本看不见，\n"
"而正确的等价概念必须忽略它。\n"
"\n"
"所以本世界讲的是挑对关系：条件等价、迹包含、单向模拟、双模拟，以及弱双模拟。\n"
"它们不可互换，而挑错了正是人们最终证明出一件为真、却不是他们本来想说的事的来由。\n"
"你会看到一对系统在一个方向上相关、而在另一个方向上可证地不相关，\n"
"还会看到一对系统提供给观察者的行为完全相同，却仍然不可互换。\n"
"\n"
"开始之前的一句提醒。这些都是关于写在这里的 Lean 模型的陈述，不关于别的任何东西。\n"
"「这个基于列表的栈精化这个计数器」的证明，不是关于任何 C 或 Rust 程序的证明；\n"
"而一个「坏操作干脆没有转移」的模型，对真实语言在程序执行这种操作时会做什么只字未言。"

#: Game.lean:10
msgid "Introduction to Program Verification"
msgstr "程序验证入门"

#. §0: `intro`
#. §1: `exact`
#. §2: `rw`
#. §3: `simp`
#: Game.lean:12
msgid "Most programmers test. This game is about the other thing you can do: **prove**.\n"
"\n"
"You will start by describing what a program *does* — states, transitions, runs — then learn to\n"
"say what it *should* do, then prove that it does. The examples stay small on purpose; the\n"
"arguments are the point, and the arguments are the ones that scale.\n"
"\n"
"Along the way you will use [CSlib](https://github.com/leanprover/cslib), Lean's library of\n"
"computer-science abstractions. You will work with automata and labelled transition systems,\n"
"apply theorems to prove invariants, verify algorithm correctness, and explore simulation and\n"
"refinement. Part of the lesson is *why* a library like that is worth having — twice in the core\n"
"path you will get a theorem for nothing that would otherwise have cost you an induction.\n"
"\n"
"**The core path** is Worlds 1 to 4. **World 5 is optional**: it opens once you have met\n"
"transition systems in World 3, and asks when one implementation may replace another.\n"
"\n"
"No prior formal-methods, automata or CSlib knowledge is assumed. Some basic Lean tactic\n"
"experience will help: §0, §1, §2, §3, and elementary induction."
msgstr "大多数程序员靠测试。这个游戏讲的是你还能做的另一件事：**证明**。\n"
"\n"
"你会先描述一个程序*做了什么*——状态、转移、运行——再学着说清它*应当*做什么，\n"
"然后证明它确实如此。例子刻意保持短小；要害在论证，而能够放大的正是论证。\n"
"\n"
"一路上你会用到 [CSlib](https://github.com/leanprover/cslib)，Lean 的计算机科学抽象库。\n"
"你会使用自动机与带标号转移系统，运用定理证明不变式，验证算法的正确性，\n"
"并探索模拟与精化。这一课有一部分是*为什么*这样一个库值得拥有——\n"
"在核心路线上你会有两次白得一条定理，而若没有它，这条定理本要花你一次归纳。\n"
"\n"
"**核心路线**是第 1 到第 4 世界。**第 5 世界是可选的**：\n"
"你在第 3 世界见过转移系统之后它就会开启，所问的是一个实现何时可以替换另一个。\n"
"\n"
"不预设任何形式化方法、自动机或 CSlib 的基础。有一点 Lean 策略的经验会有帮助：\n"
"§0、§1、§2、§3，以及初等的归纳。"

